[0.000, "o", "?7h\u001b[116G\u001b[?7l\r\n\n\n\u001b[K  ❓ \u001b[1mQ5\u001b[m - \u001b[1mBuild Lifecycle & Notes\u001b[m: Beyond the BOM parts list, what does tracking a \"DIY kit build\" involve for you—tr\u001b[?7h\u001b[118G\n\u001b[103D\u001b[90m.\u001b[94m.\u001b[m\n\n\n\u001b[14D\u001b[?2026l"]
[0.018, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\r\u001b[29A  ➡️ A Kit Build has a Bill of Materials (BOM) that links to your Component inventory so you can check build\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[?5W\u001b[J  readiness (\"can I build this with what's in my bins?\"), allocate/consume stock when building, and generate a\r\n  shopping list for missing parts.\r\n  ──────\u001b[?7l\r\n\u001b[K  ❓ \u001b[1mQ2\u001b[m - \u001b[1mAudio electronics domain specifics\u001b[m: Audio DIY involves domain-specific nuances—like resistor/capacitor\u001b[?7h\u001b[113G\r\n  tolerances, voltage ratings, package types (Through-Hole vs. SMD), matched pairs (e.g., transistors/JFETs), IC\r\n  pinouts, or kits that come with partial parts vs. bare PCBs. Should the component catalog use structured parametric\r\n  attributes by category (e.g., Resistance, Capacitance, Package, Value) or simple freeform tags/fields?\u001b[?7l\r\n\n\u001b[K  ➡️ Structured parametric attributes for common electronics categories (Resistors, Capacitors, Semiconductors/ICs,\u001b[?7h\u001b[116G\r\n  Potentiometers/Switches, Hardware/Connectors, Bare PCBs/Kits) plus physical storage"]
[0.000, "o", " location (bin/drawer).\r\n  ──────\u001b[?7l\r\n\u001b[K  ❓ \u001b[1mQ3\u001b[m - \u001b[1mDeployment & Data Ownership\u001b[m: Is this a personal, single-user tool running locally (or self-hosted on your\u001b[?7h\u001b[116G\r\n  LAN with a local database like SQLite), or a multi-user cloud web app with accounts and authentication?\u001b[?7l\r\n\n\u001b[K  ➡️ A single-user, local-first / self-hosted web application backed by a local database (e.g., SQLite) with easy\u001b[?7h\u001b[114G\r\n  backup/export, avoiding unnecessary auth and cloud infrastructure complexity.\r\n  ──────\u001b[?7l\r\n\u001b[K  ❓ \u001b[1mQ4\u001b[m - \u001b[1mSupplier & BOM Import / Lookup\u001b[m: How do you expect data to enter the system? Will you mostly enter parts and\u001b[?7h\u001b[118G\r\n  BOMs manually / via CSV import, or do you want automated part lookup/scraping from suppliers (like Mouser, DigiKey,\r\n  Tayda, LCSC)?\u001b[?7l\r\n\n\u001b[K  ➡️ Support manual entry and CSV/spreadsheet import for BOMs and inventory first, keeping third-party supplier API\u001b[?7h\u001b[116G\r\n  integrations (Mouser/DigiKey) either optional"]
[0.000, "o", " or out of scope for the initial spec.\r\n  ──────\u001b[?7l\r\n\u001b[K  ❓ \u001b[1mQ5\u001b[m - \u001b[1mBuild Lifecycle & Notes\u001b[m: Beyond the BOM parts list, what does tracking a \"DIY kit build\" involve for\u001b[?7h\u001b[111G\r\n  you—tracking build\r\n⣽  \u001b[90mGenerating..\u001b[94m.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[90m└ Tip: Use /model to switch between available models.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[90m────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[94m>\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[90m──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────"]
