[0.000, "o", "for BOMs and inventory first, keeping third-party supplier API\u001b[?7h\u001b[116G\r\n  integrations (Mouser/DigiKey) either optional or out of scope for the initial spec.\r\n  ──────\u001b[?7l\r\n\u001b[K  ❓ \u001b[1mQ5\u001b[m - \u001b[1mBuild Lifecycle & Notes\u001b[m: Beyond the BOM parts list, what does tracking a \"DIY kit build\" involve for\u001b[?7h\u001b[111G\r\n  you—tracking build status stages (e.g., Planned, Sourcing, Ready to Build, In Progress, Troubleshooting,\r\n  Completed), build logs/notes, schematic/build-doc attachments, or calibration/test measurements?\u001b[?7l\r\n\u001b[K\u001b[?7h\u001b[1G\u001b[?7l\n\u001b[K  ➡️ Track build status stages, BOM sourcing/allocation state, build notes/troubleshooting logs, and\u001b[?7h\u001b[101G\r\n  links/attachments for schematics and build docs.\u001b[K\u001b[?7l\r\n\n\u001b[K\u001b[90m────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[?7h\u001b[61G\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[34;1m> one question at a time\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[?7l\r\n\n\u001b[K  ❓ \u001b[1mQ1\u001b[?7h\u001b[8G\u001b[m\r\n⣾"]
