[0.000, "o", "────────\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[34;1m> one question at a time\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[K\u001b[?7l\n\u001b[K  ❓ \u001b[1mQ1\u001b[m - \u001b[1mCore domain relationship between Inventory and Kit Builds\u001b[m: How do components in your inventory relate to\u001b[?7h\u001b[115G\r\n  DIY kit builds? Specifically, is a \u001b[1mKit Build\u001b[m defined by a Bill of Materials (BOM) that checks against and/or\u001b[?7l\r\n\u001b[K  deducts from your \u001b[1mComponent\u001b[m stock (telling you what you have on hand vs. what you need to buy for a build), or are\u001b[?7h\u001b[117G\r\n  kits tracked mostly as independent project logs?\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\u001b[?7l\n\u001b[K  ➡️ A Kit Build has a Bill of Materials (BOM) that links to your Component inventory so you can check build\u001b[?7h\u001b[109G\r\n  readiness (\"can I build this with what's in my bins?\"), allocate/consume stock when building, and generate a\u001b[?7l\r\n\u001b[K  shopping list for missing parts.\u001b[?7h\u001b[35G\r\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[90m───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────"]
[0.000, "o", "─\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[34;1m> yes\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[K\u001b[?7l\n\u001b[K  ❓ \u001b[1mQ2\u001b[?7h\u001b[8G\u001b[m\n\b\u001b[94md\u001b[90mi\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[90m└ Tip: View and review artifacts with /artifact.\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[90m────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[94m>\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[90m────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[90mesc to cancel\u001b[m\u001b[84X\u001b[84C\u001b[2mGemini 4 Argon · medium\u001b[m\r\u001b[2A\u001b[2C\u001b[?2026l"]
[0.017, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\r\u001b[29A  Tayda, LCSC)?\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[?5W\u001b[J\u001b[?7l\u001b[K  ➡️ Support manual entry and CSV/spreadsheet import for BOMs and inventory first, keeping third-party supplier API\u001b[?7h\u001b[116G\r\n  integrations (Mouser/DigiKey) either optional or out of scope for the initial spec.\r\n  ──────\u001b[?7l\r\n\u001b[K  ❓ \u001b[1mQ5\u001b[m - \u001b[1mBuild Lifecycle & Notes\u001b[m: Beyond the BOM parts list, what does tracking a \"DIY kit build\" involve for\u001b[?7h\u001b[111G\r\n  you—tracking build status stages (e.g., Planned, Sourcing, Ready to Build, In Progress, Troubleshooting,\r\n  Completed), build logs/notes, schematic/build-doc attachments, or calibration/test measurements?\u001b[?7l\r\n\n\u001b[K  ➡️ Track build status stages, BOM sourcing/allocation state, build notes/troubleshooting logs, and\u001b[?7h\u001b[101G\r\n  links/attachments for schematics and build docs.\r\n\n\u001b[90m────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[3"]
