[0.083, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\r\u001b[29A\u001b[K\r\n  ❓ \u001b[1mQ1\u001b[m - \u001b[1mCore domain relationship between Inventory and Kit Builds\u001b[m: How do components in your inventory relate to\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[?5W\u001b[J  DIY kit builds? Specifically, is a \u001b[1mKit Build\u001b[m defined by a Bill of Materials (BOM) that checks against and/or\r\n  deducts from your \u001b[1mComponent\u001b[m stock (telling you what you have on hand vs. what you need to buy for a build), or are\r\n  kits tracked mostly as independent project logs?\u001b[?7l\r\n\n\u001b[K  ➡️ A Kit Build has a Bill of Materials (BOM) that links to your Component inventory so you can check build\u001b[?7h\u001b[109G\r\n  readiness (\"can I build this with what's in my bins?\"), allocate/consume stock when building, and generate a\r\n  shopping list for missing parts.\r\n\n\u001b[90m────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[34;1m> yes\u001b[?7l\u001b[m\r\n\n\u001b[K  ❓ \u001b[1mQ2\u001b[m - \u001b[1mAudio electronics domain specifics\u001b[m: Audio D"]
