[0.050, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\r\u001b[29A\u001b[K\r\n  ➡️ A Kit Build has a Bill of Materials (BOM) that links to your Component inventory so you can check build\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[?5W\u001b[J  readiness (\"can I build this with what's in my bins?\"), allocate/consume stock when building, and generate a\r\n  shopping list for missing parts.\r\n\n\u001b[90m────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[34;1m> yes\u001b[?7l\u001b[m\r\n\n\u001b[K  ❓ \u001b[1mQ2\u001b[m - \u001b[1mAudio electronics domain specifics\u001b[m: Audio DIY involves domain-specific nuances—like resistor/capacitor\u001b[?7h\u001b[113G\r\n  tolerances, voltage ratings, package types (Through-Hole vs. SMD), matched pairs (e.g., transistors/JFETs), or kits\r\n  that come as bare PCBs vs. partial/full kits. Should the component catalog use structured parametric attributes by\r\n  category (e.g., Resistance, Capacitance, Package, Value) plus storage location, or simple freeform tags/fields?\u001b[?7l\r\n\n\u001b[K  ➡️ Str"]
[0.000, "o", "uctured parametric attributes for common electronics categories (Resistors, Capacitors, Semiconductors/ICs,\u001b[?7h\u001b[116G\r\n  Potentiometers/Switches, Hardware/Connectors, Enclosures/PCBs) plus physical storage location (bin/drawer).\r\n\n\u001b[90m────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[34;1m> structured\u001b[?7l\u001b[m\r\n\n\u001b[K  ❓ \u001b[1mQ3\u001b[m - \u001b[1mDeployment & Data Ownership\u001b[m: Is this a personal, single-user tool running locally (or self-hosted on your\u001b[?7h\u001b[116G\r\n  LAN with a local database like SQLite), or a multi-user cloud web app with accounts and authentication?\u001b[?7l\r\n\n\u001b[K  ➡️ A single-user, local-first / self-hosted web application backed by a local database (e.g., SQLite) with easy\u001b[?7h\u001b[114G\r\n  backup/export, avoiding unnecessary auth and cloud infrastructure complexity.\r\n\n\u001b[90m───────────────────────────────"]
