[0.018, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\r\u001b[29A\u001b[K\r\n  ❓ \u001b[1mQ5\u001b[m - \u001b[1mBuild Lifecycle & Notes\u001b[m: Beyond the BOM parts list, what does tracking a \"DIY kit build\" involve for\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[?5W\u001b[J  you—tracking build status stages (e.g., Planned, Sourcing, Ready to Build, In Progress, Troubleshooting,\r\n  Completed), build logs/notes, schematic/build-doc attachments, or calibration/test measurements?\u001b[?7l\r\n\n\u001b[K  ➡️ Track build status stages, BOM sourcing/allocation state, build notes/troubleshooting logs, and\u001b[?7h\u001b[101G\r\n  links/attachments for schematics and build docs.\r\n\n\u001b[90m────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[34;1m> yes please\u001b[?7l\u001b[m\r\n\n\u001b[K  ❓ \u001b[1mQ6\u001b[m - \u001b[1mProject vs. Build instance (Domain terminology)\u001b[m: In DIY audio (like Eurorack modules, guitar pedals, or\u001b[?7h\u001b[114G\r\n  synth kits), sometimes you have a reusable kit/circuit design (with its BOM and build docs) that you might build"]
[0.000, "o", "\r\n  once or multiple times—or you might treat each build as a single object with its own BOM. Should we distinguish\r\n  between a reusable \u001b[1mProject / Kit Template\u001b[m (which holds the canonical BOM and docs) and a \u001b[1mBuild\u001b[m (an actual instance\r\n  you are sourcing and soldering), or keep them merged as a single \u001b[1mKit Build\u001b[m concept?\u001b[?7l\r\n\n\u001b[K  ➡️ Keep them merged as a single \u001b[1mProject Build\u001b[m (with an easy \"Clone / Duplicate Build\" action if you ever build a\u001b[?7h\u001b[115G\r\n  second unit of the same kit), unless you regularly build multiple units of the same design simultaneously.\r\n\n\u001b[90m────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[34;1m> single concept, I'm not a serial maufacturer, just a hobby builder\u001b[m\r\n\n\u001b[32m●\u001b[m \u001b[33;1mEdited\u001b[m 1 file \u001b[37m(GLOSSARY.md)\u001b[m \u001b[37m(ctrl+o to expand)\u001b[?7l\u001b[m\r\n\n\u001b[K  ❓ \u001b[1mQ7\u001b[m - \u001b[1mTech Stack & Runtime Preferences\u001b"]
