[0.025, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\r\u001b[29A\u001b[K\u001b[?7l\n\u001b[K  ❓ \u001b[1mQ6\u001b[m - \u001b[1mProject vs. Build instance (Domain terminology)\u001b[m: In DIY audio (like Eurorack modules, guitar pedals, or\u001b[?7h\u001b[114G\u001b[?7l\r\n\u001b[K  synth kits), sometimes you have a reusable kit/circuit design (with its BOM and build docs) that you might build\u001b[?7h\u001b[115G\r\n  once or multiple times—or you might treat each build as a single object with its own BOM. Should we distinguish\u001b[K\r\n  between a reusable \u001b[1mProject / Kit Template\u001b[m (which holds the canonical BOM and docs) and a \u001b[1mBuild\u001b[m (an actual instance\r\n  you are sourcing and soldering), or keep them merged as a single \u001b[1mKit Build\u001b[m concept?\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\u001b[?7l\n\u001b[K  ➡️ Keep them merged as a single \u001b[1mProject Build\u001b[m (with an easy \"Clone / Duplicate Build\" action if you ever build a\u001b[?7h\u001b[115G\u001b[?7l\r\n\u001b[K  second unit of the same kit), unless you regularly build multiple units of the same design simultaneously.\u001b[?7h\u001b[109G\r\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[90m────────────────────────────"]
[0.000, "o", "────────────────────────────────\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[34;1m> single concept, I'm not a serial maufacturer, just a hobby builder\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[32m●\u001b[m \u001b[33;1mEdited\u001b[m 1 file \u001b[37m(GLOSSARY.md)\u001b[m \u001b[37m(ctrl+o to expand)\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[K\u001b[?7l\n\u001b[K  ❓ \u001b[1mQ7\u001b[m - \u001b[1mTech Stack & Runtime Preferences\u001b[m: Before I chart the wayfinding map and its decision tickets, do you have\u001b[?7h\u001b[116G\u001b[?7l\r\n\u001b[K  an existing preference for the web stack (e.g., TypeScript with Next.js / Remix / Vite + React + SQLite via\u001b[?7h\u001b[110G\r\n  Drizzle/Prisma, or something else), or should choosing the tech stack be one of the decision tickets on the map?\r\n\u001b[K\u001b[?7l\n\u001b[K  ➡️ Make \u001b[1mTech Stack & Local Persistence Architecture\u001b[m an explicit decision ticket on the frontier of the map so we\u001b[?7h\u001b[115G\u001b[?7l\r\n\u001b[K  can weigh options (or lock in your preferred stack) cleanly.\u001b[?7h\u001b[63G\r\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[90m─────────────────────────────────────"]
