[0.000, "o", "─────────────\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[34;1m> single concept, I'm not a serial maufacturer, just a hobby builder\u001b[m\r\n\n\u001b[32m●\u001b[m \u001b[33;1mEdited\u001b[m 1 file \u001b[37m(GLOSSARY.md)\u001b[m \u001b[37m(ctrl+o to expand)\u001b[?7l\u001b[m\r\n\n\u001b[K  ❓ \u001b[1mQ7\u001b[m - \u001b[1mTech Stack & Runtime Preferences\u001b[m: Before I chart the wayfinding map and its decision tickets, do you have\u001b[?7h\u001b[116G\r\n  an existing preference for the web stack (e.g., TypeScript with Next.js / Remix / Vite + React + SQLite via\r\n  Drizzle/Prisma, or something else), or should choosing the tech stack be one of the decision tickets on the map?\u001b[?7l\r\n\n\u001b[K  ➡️ Make \u001b[1mTech Stack & Local Persistence Architecture\u001b[m an explicit decision ticket on the frontier of the map so we\u001b[?7h\u001b[115G\r\n  can weigh options (or lock in your preferred stack) cleanly.\r\n\n\u001b[90m────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[34;1m> I have tech preferences\u001b"]
