[0.000, "o", "3)\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[33m○\u001b[m \u001b[33;1mEditing\u001b[m 1 file \u001b[37m(05-core-ui-views-and-htmx-interaction-prototype.md)\u001b[m \u001b[37m(ctrl+o to expand)\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[33;1mCreate file\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[90m────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[37;1m/Users/brett/Demos/audio-inventory-experiment/audio_inventory_skilled/docs/adr/0001-rust-htmx-turso-stack.md\u001b[m  \u001b[32m+3\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[37m  \u001b[90m1 \u001b[39;48;2;14;52;15m \u001b[32m+  \u001b[39m# Rust Backend, Server-Rendered HTML with HTMX, and Local Turso Database\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[37m  \u001b[90m2 \u001b[39;48;2;14;52;15m \u001b[32m+  \u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[?7l\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[K\u001b[37m  \u001b[90m3 \u001b[39;48;2;14;52;15m \u001b[32m+  \u001b[39mWe are building the audio electronics inventory and DIY kit build tracker as a single-user, local-first web     \u001b[?"]
[0.000, "o", "7h\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[37m    \u001b[48;2;14;52;15m \u001b[32m   \u001b[39mapplication using a Rust backend serving server-rendered HTML augmented with HTMX, persisted in a local Turso\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[37m    \u001b[48;2;14;52;15m \u001b[32m   \u001b[39m(libSQL) database. This stack keeps runtime overhead minimal, avoids client-side SPA state synchronization\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[37m    \u001b[48;2;14;52;15m \u001b[32m   \u001b[39mcomplexity for tabular/form-heavy inventory workflows, and provides a single self-contained binary with\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[37m    \u001b[48;2;14;52;15m \u001b[32m   \u001b[39membedded/local SQL storage.\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[1mAllow creation of this file?\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[94m> 1. Yes, allow creation\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n  2. No, deny creation\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\n  \u001b[94;1m↑/↓\u001b[90;22m Navigate · \u001b[94;1mtab\u001b[90;22m Amend · \u001b[94;1mf\u001b[90;22m full diff\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[?2026l"]
[37.846, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\r\u001b[30A  Also, would you like me to record an initial ADR (\u001b[94mdocs/adr/0001-rust-htmx-turso-stack.md\u001b[m) for the Rust + server-\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[?5W\u001b[0 q\u001b[J  rendered HTML/HTMX + local Turso stack?\r\n\n  \u001b[1mProposed Frontier & Blocked Decision Tickets:\u001b[m\r\n\n  1. \u001b[1mComponent Category Taxonomy & Parametric Schema\u001b[m (\u001b[94mgrilling\u001b[m, unblocked): Define the exact categories, structured\r\n  attributes, value normalization/units (e.g., \u001b[94m4k7\u001b[m vs \u001b[94m4700Ω\u001b[m), and storage location model.\r\n  2. \u001b[1mBOM Matching, Stock Allocation, and Build Lifecycle\u001b[m (\u001b[94mgrilling\u001b[m, blocked by \u001b[94m01\u001b[m): Decide how BOM lines match\r\n  against \u001b[94mComponent\u001b[m stock (exact part vs. parametric spec match, handling partial kits where some parts come in the\r\n  box), when stock is reserved vs. deducted, and exact \u001b[94mKit Build\u001b[m status transitions.\r\n  3. \u001b[1mCSV Import & Shopping List Export Workflows\u001b[m (\u001b[94mgrilling\u001b[m, blocked by \u001b[94m02\u001b[m): Define how messy BOM/inventory CSVs are\r\n  mapped/reconciled on import and h"]
