[0.016, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\u001b[29AI have loaded the \u001b[34;4m\u001b]8;id=jk24c34ba89d263809;file:///Users/brett/Demos/audio-inventory-experiment/audio_inventory_skilled/.scratch/audio-inventory/map.md\u0007Audio Electronics Inventory & Kit Builds Map\u001b[m\u001b]8;;\u0007 and claimed the first open frontier ticket:\r\n  **\u001b[34;4m\u001b]8;id=jk16391497558c00bc;file:///Users/brett/Demos/audio-inventory-experiment/audio_inventory_skilled/.scratch/audio-inventory/issues/01-component-category-taxonomy-and-parametric-schema.md\u0007Component Category Taxonomy & Parametric Schema\u001b[m\u001b]8;;\u0007**.\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\n  Let's resolve the decisions for this ticket one question at a time.\r\n  ──────\u001b[K\u001b[?7l\r\n\u001b[K  ❓ \u001b[1mQ1\u001b[m - \u001b[1mComponent Category Taxonomy\u001b[m: What set of top-level \u001b[1mComponent Categories\u001b[m should the catalog support, and\u001b[?7h\u001b[114G\u001b[?7l\r\n\u001b[K  should categories be a fixed built-in set (each with tailored parametric fields) or user-extensible?\u001b[?7h\u001b[103G\r\n\u001b[K\n  For a DIY audio electronics bench (guitar pedals, synth modules, amplifiers), a two-level or flat bui"]
[0.000, "o", "lt-in taxonomy\r\n  tailored to audio builds covers nearly everything while allowing category-specific parametric attributes:\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\n  1. \u001b[1mResistors\u001b[m (Fixed resistors, trimmer/preset resistors, resistor networks/arrays)\r\n  2. \u001b[1mCapacitors\u001b[m (Film, ceramic, electrolytic, tantalum, mica, trimmer)\u001b[K\r\n  3. \u001b[1mSemiconductors — Discrete\u001b[m (Diodes, LEDs, BJTs, JFETs, MOSFETs — including matched pairs/quads and vintage\r\n  germanium/silicon transistors)\u001b[K\r\n  4. \u001b[1mIntegrated Circuits (ICs)\u001b[m (Op-amps, logic, PT2399/BBD delay, voltage regulators, Specialized audio/synth ICs,\r\n  optocouplers/vactrols)\u001b[K\r\n  5. \u001b[1mPotentiometers & Encoders\u001b[m (Rotary pots, slide pots, multi-turn pots, rotary encoders)\r\n  6. \u001b[1mSwitches, Jacks & Connectors\u001b[m (Footswitches, toggle/push/rotary/DIP switches, 1/4\" & 3.5mm audio jacks, DC power\r\n  jacks, pin headers/sockets, IC sockets)\u001b[K\r\n  7. \u001b[1mInductors, Transformers & Magnetics\u001b[m (Audio transformers, power transformers, inductors/chokes, wah inductors)\r\n  8. \u001b[1mEnc"]
[0.000, "o", "losures, Knobs & Mechanical Hardware\u001b[m (Hammond/1590 enclosures, knobs, standoffs, nuts/washers/screws,\u001b[K\r\n  PCBs/stripboard, wire, solder)\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\u001b[?7l\n\u001b[K  ➡️ \u001b[1mRecommended\u001b[m: Use a \u001b[1mbuilt-in set of these 8 core categories\u001b[m (with a subtype field per category, e.g., \u001b[94mFilm\u001b[m vs\u001b[?7h\u001b[114G\u001b[?7l\r\n\u001b[K  \u001b[94mElectrolytic\u001b[m capacitor, or \u001b[94mJFET\u001b[m vs \u001b[94mBJT\u001b[m discrete semiconductor) plus an optional \u001b[1m\"Other / Custom\"\u001b[m category so every\u001b[?7h\u001b[117G\r\n  standar\u001b[K\n\n\n\u001b[7D\u001b[?2026l"]
