[0.016, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\u001b[?7l\r\u001b[28A\u001b[K  ➡️ \u001b[1mRecommended\u001b[m: Implement the \u001b[1mdeterministic Electrical Value Parser & Normalizer\u001b[m for resistance, capacitance,\u001b[?7h\u001b[112G\u001b[?7l\r\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\u001b[K  ❓ \u001b[1mQ4\u001b[m - \u001b[1mPhysical Storage Locations\u001b[m: How do you organize parts on your bench/workshop (e.g., Akro-Mils drawer\u001b[?7h\u001b[111G\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\u001b[7D\u001b[94mx 3: Pots & \u001b[m\r\n\n\n\n\n\u001b[2C\u001b[?2026l"]
[0.018, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\u001b[?7l\r\u001b[29A\u001b[K  ➡️ \u001b[1mRecommended\u001b[m: Implement the \u001b[1mdeterministic Electrical Value Parser & Normalizer\u001b[m for resistance, capacitance,\u001b[?7h\u001b[112G\u001b[?7l\r\n\u001b[K  inductance, voltage, and potentiometer taper-value codes (\u001b[94mA100k\u001b[m/\u001b[94m100kA\u001b[m), storing canonical numeric columns\u001b[?7h\u001b[108G\r\n  (\u001b[94mresistance_ohms\u001b[m, \u001b[94mcapacitance_pf\u001b[m, \u001b[94minductance_uh\u001b[m, \u001b[94mvoltage_rating_volts\u001b[m) and formatting capacitance in the \u001b[94m1nF–999nF\u001b[m\r\n  range as \u001b[94mnF\u001b[m by default. Does this match how you want value entry and search to behave?\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[90m────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[34;1m> I'd like to store the original spec string alongside a canonicalized value. A lot of the values include additional\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[34;1m  information, like variance and pot curve that are important\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\n  That's a crucial distinction—preserving the \u001b[1mr"]
[0.000, "o", "aw spec string\u001b[m (e.g., \u001b[94m100kA 16mm\u001b[m, \u001b[94m4k7 1% 1/4W\u001b[m, \u001b[94m0.047uF 63V Box\u001b[m, \u001b[94mB50K\u001b[m\r\n  \u001b[94mCenter Detent\u001b[m) verbatim alongside the extracted/canonicalized numeric and parametric fields ensures nothing entered\r\n  or imported from a schematic/BOM is ever lost, while still enabling normalized numeric search, sorting, and BOM\u001b[K\r\n  matching.\u001b[K\r\n  ──────\u001b[K\u001b[?7l\r\n\u001b[K  ❓ \u001b[1mQ4\u001b[m - \u001b[1mPhysical Storage Locations\u001b[m: How do you organize parts on your bench/workshop (e.g., Akro-Mils drawer\u001b[?7h\u001b[111G\u001b[?7l\r\n\u001b[K  cabinets, resistor/capacitor component binders with pages/sleeves, SMD books, tackle boxes, shelf bins), and should\u001b[?7h\u001b[118G\r\n  a \u001b[1mStorage Location\u001b[m be a structured hierarchical entity (e.g., \u001b[94mContainer > Drawer/Page/Slot\u001b[m like \u001b[94mCabinet A > Row 3\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n  \u001b[94mCol 2\u001b[m or \u001b[94mResistor Binder > Page 4\u001b[m) or a flat label/code? Also, can a single \u001b[1mComponent\u001b[m live in only one storage\u001b[K\r\n  location, or split across multiple locations (e.g., working benc"]
