[0.017, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\u001b[?7l\r\u001b[23A\u001b[K  ❓ \u001b[1mQ4\u001b[m - \u001b[1mPhysical Storage Locations\u001b[m: How do you organize parts on your bench/workshop (e.g., Akro-Mils drawer\u001b[?7h\u001b[111G\u001b[?7l\r\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\u001b[K  ➡️ \u001b[1mRecommended\u001b[m: Model \u001b[1mStorage Location\u001b[m as a \u001b[1mStorage Container\u001b[m entity (with name, type like \u001b[94mDrawe\u001b[?7h\u001b[99G\u001b[m\n\n\n\n\u001b[96D\u001b[?2026l"]
[0.017, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\u001b[?7l\r\u001b[23A\u001b[K  ❓ \u001b[1mQ4\u001b[m - \u001b[1mPhysical Storage Locations\u001b[m: How do you organize parts on your bench/workshop (e.g., Akro-Mils drawer\u001b[?7h\u001b[111G\u001b[?7l\r\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\u001b[K  ➡️ \u001b[1mRecommended\u001b[m: Model \u001b[1mStorage Location\u001b[m as a \u001b[1mStorage Container\u001b[m entity (with name, type like \u001b[94mDrawer Cabinet\u001b[m /\u001b[?7h\u001b[110G\n\u001b[97D\u001b[90m.\u001b[m\n\n\n\u001b[11D\u001b[?2026l"]
[0.016, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\u001b[29AThat's a crucial distinction—preserving the \u001b[1mraw spec string\u001b[m (e.g., \u001b[94m100kA 16mm\u001b[m, \u001b[94m4k7 1% 1/4W\u001b[m, \u001b[94m0.047uF 63V Box\u001b[m, \u001b[94mB50K\u001b[m\r\n  \u001b[94mCenter Detent\u001b[m) verbatim alongside the extracted/canonicalized numeric and parametric fields ensures nothing entered\r\n  or imported from a schematic/BOM is ever lost, while still enabling normalized numeric search, sorting, and BOM\u001b[K\r\n  matching.\u001b[K\r\n  ──────\u001b[K\u001b[?7l\r\n\u001b[K  ❓ \u001b[1mQ4\u001b[m - \u001b[1mPhysical Storage Locations\u001b[m: How do you organize parts on your bench/workshop (e.g., Akro-Mils drawer\u001b[?7h\u001b[111G\u001b[?7l\r\n\u001b[K  cabinets, resistor/capacitor component binders with pages/sleeves, SMD books, tackle boxes, shelf bins), and should\u001b[?7h\u001b[118G\r\n  a \u001b[1mStorage Location\u001b[m be a structured hierarchical entity (e.g., \u001b[94mContainer > Drawer/Page/Slot\u001b[m like \u001b[94mCabinet A > Row 3\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n  \u001b[94mCol 2\u001b[m or \u001b[94mResistor Binder > Page 4\u001b[m) or a flat label/code? Also, can a single \u001b[1mComponent\u001b[m live in only one storage\u001b[K\r\n  "]
[0.000, "o", "location, or split across multiple locations (e.g., working bench drawer + bulk overflow bin)?\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\n  Let's compare the two main models:\r\n\u001b[K\n  1. \u001b[1mSingle Primary Location per Component + Two-Level Hierarchy (\u001b[94;22mStorage Container\u001b[39;1m → \u001b[94;22mSlot / Label\u001b[39;1m)\u001b[m:\r\n      • You define \u001b[1mStorage Containers\u001b[m (e.g., \u001b[94mBinder 1: 1/4W Metal Film\u001b[m, \u001b[94mCabinet A: IC & Transistors\u001b[m, \u001b[94mBox 3: Pots &\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[6C\u001b[94mJacks\u001b[m, \u001b[94mShelf: Enclosures & Modules\u001b[m) and each \u001b[1mComponent\u001b[m has a \u001b[94mcontainer_id\u001b[m + a freeform \u001b[94mslot_label\u001b[m (e.g., \u001b[94mPage 3,\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[6C\u001b[94mRow 2\u001b[m, \u001b[94mDrawer B4\u001b[m, \u001b[94mBag 12\u001b[m) plus an optional \u001b[94moverflow_location\u001b[m note.\u001b[K\n\u001b[66D• Keeping a single \u001b[94mquantity_on_hand\u001b[m and primary location (\u001b[94mContainer\u001b[m + \u001b[94mSlot\u001b[m) per Component makes inline \u001b[94m+1 / -1\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[6Cstock adjustments and BOM part-pulling instant without asking \u001b[3m\"which bin are you taking this 10k resistor\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[6C\u001b[3mfrom?\"\u001b[m every time you build a kit.\u001b"]
[0.000, "o", "[K\r\n  2. \u001b[1mMulti-Location Stock Balances (Many-to-Many \u001b[94;22mComponent\u001b[39;1m ↔ \u001b[94;22mStorage Location\u001b[39;1m with separate quantities per bin)\u001b[m:\r\n      • Every stock adjustment or BOM consumption requires choosing which location's balance to decrement.\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\u001b[?7l\n\n\u001b[K  ➡️ \u001b[1mRecommended\u001b[m: Model \u001b[1mStorage Location\u001b[m as a \u001b[1mStorage Container\u001b[m entity (with name, type like \u001b[94mDrawer Cabinet\u001b[m / \u001b[94mBinder\u001b[?7h\u001b[117G\u001b[?7l\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[K  /\u001b[?7h\u001b[4G\r\n⣾ \n\n\n\u001b[?2026l"]
