[0.099, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\u001b[?7l\r\u001b[15A\u001b[K  ➡️ \u001b[1mRecommended\u001b[m: Model \u001b[1mStorage Location\u001b[m as a \u001b[1mStorage Container\u001b[m entity (with name, type like \u001b[94mDrawer Cabinet\u001b[m / \u001b[94mBinder\u001b[?7h\u001b[117G\u001b[m\r\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n⢿  \u001b[94mLoad\u001b[m\n\n\n\u001b[5D\u001b[?2026l"]
[0.067, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\u001b[29ALet's compare the two main models:\r\n\u001b[K\n  1. \u001b[1mSingle Primary Location per Component + Two-Level Hierarchy (\u001b[94;22mStorage Container\u001b[39;1m → \u001b[94;22mSlot / Label\u001b[39;1m)\u001b[m:\r\n      • You define \u001b[1mStorage Containers\u001b[m (e.g., \u001b[94mBinder 1: 1/4W Metal Film\u001b[m, \u001b[94mCabinet A: IC & Transistors\u001b[m, \u001b[94mBox 3: Pots &\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[6C\u001b[94mJacks\u001b[m, \u001b[94mShelf: Enclosures & Modules\u001b[m) and each \u001b[1mComponent\u001b[m has a \u001b[94mcontainer_id\u001b[m + a freeform \u001b[94mslot_label\u001b[m (e.g., \u001b[94mPage 3,\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[6C\u001b[94mRow 2\u001b[m, \u001b[94mDrawer B4\u001b[m, \u001b[94mBag 12\u001b[m) plus an optional \u001b[94moverflow_location\u001b[m note.\u001b[K\n\u001b[66D• Keeping a single \u001b[94mquantity_on_hand\u001b[m and primary location (\u001b[94mContainer\u001b[m + \u001b[94mSlot\u001b[m) per Component makes inline \u001b[94m+1 / -1\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[6Cstock adjustments and BOM part-pulling instant without asking \u001b[3m\"which bin are you taking this 10k resistor\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[6C\u001b[3mfrom?\"\u001b[m every time you build a kit.\u001b[K\r\n  2. \u001b[1mMulti-Location Stock Balances (Many-to-Many \u001b[94;22mComponent\u001b[39;1m ↔ \u001b[94;2"]
[0.000, "o", "2mStorage Location\u001b[39;1m with separate quantities per bin)\u001b[m:\r\n      • Every stock adjustment or BOM consumption requires choosing which location's balance to decrement.\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\u001b[?7l\n\n\u001b[K  ➡️ \u001b[1mRecommended\u001b[m: Model \u001b[1mStorage Location\u001b[m as a \u001b[1mStorage Container\u001b[m entity (with name, type like \u001b[94mDrawer Cabinet\u001b[m / \u001b[94mBinder\u001b[?7h\u001b[117G\u001b[?7l\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[K  / \u001b[94mBox\u001b[m / \u001b[94mShelf\u001b[m, and description) paired with a \u001b[94mslot_label\u001b[m on the Component (plus an optional\u001b[?7h\u001b[94G\r\n  \u001b[94msecondary_location_notes\u001b[m field), keeping a single \u001b[94mquantity_on_hand\u001b[m per Component so stock adjustments and kit\r\n  kitting stay one-click fast. Does this match how your physical storage works?\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[90m────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[34;1m> I currently have a mixture of boxes with parts like partially assembled kits, crates with bags of components, "]
[0.001, "o", "and in\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[34;1m  some cases I have crates with bags full of bagged components. Given I need to move the bags of components around it\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[2C\u001b[34;1mis probably worth having a heirarichal concept for storage\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\n  That makes total sense: if you have a \u001b[1mCrate\u001b[m containing large \u001b[1mBags\u001b[m or \u001b[1mBoxes\u001b[m, which in turn contain smaller \u001b[1mBags\u001b[m of\r\n  components (or partially assembled kits), and you move a whole bag from one crate/box to another, a true \u001b[1mself-\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n  \u001b[1mreferential hierarchy (\u001b[94;22mparent_\u001b[m\u001b[K\n\u001b[25D\u001b[94mi\u001b[90mn\u001b[m\n\n\n\u001b[7D\u001b[?2026l"]
