[0.017, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\u001b[?7l\r\u001b[29A\u001b[K  ➡️ \u001b[1mRecommended\u001b[m: Model \u001b[1mStorage Location\u001b[m as a \u001b[1mStorage Container\u001b[m entity (with name, type like \u001b[94mDrawer Cabinet\u001b[m / \u001b[94mBinder\u001b[?7h\u001b[117G\u001b[?7l\u001b[m\r\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\u001b[K  ❓ \u001b[1mQ5\u001b[m - \u001b[1mHierarchical Storage Locations & Moving Bags\u001b[m: If we model \u001b[1mStorage Location\u001b[m as a self-referential tree (\u001b[94mid\u001b[m,\u001b[?7h\u001b[117G\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\u001b[3Zf (or interm\r\n\n\n\n\u001b[2C\u001b[?2026l"]
[0.018, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\r\u001b[29A  ➡️ \u001b[1mRecommended\u001b[m: Model \u001b[1mStorage Location\u001b[m as a \u001b[1mStorage Container\u001b[m entity (with name, type like \u001b[94mDrawer Cabinet\u001b[m / \u001b[94mBinder\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[?5W\u001b[J  / \u001b[94mBox\u001b[m / \u001b[94mShelf\u001b[m, and description) paired with a \u001b[94mslot_label\u001b[m on the Component (plus an optional\r\n  \u001b[94msecondary_location_notes\u001b[m field), keeping a single \u001b[94mquantity_on_hand\u001b[m per Component so stock adjustments and kit\r\n  kitting stay one-click fast. Does this match how your physical storage works?\r\n\n\u001b[90m────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[34;1m> I currently have a mixture of boxes with parts like partially assembled kits, crates with bags of components, and in\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[34;1m  some cases I have crates with bags full of bagged components. Given I need to move the bags of components around it\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[34;1m  is probably worth having a heirarichal concept for s"]
[0.000, "o", "torage\u001b[m\r\n\n  That makes total sense: if you have a \u001b[1mCrate\u001b[m containing large \u001b[1mBags\u001b[m or \u001b[1mBoxes\u001b[m, which in turn contain smaller \u001b[1mBags\u001b[m of\r\n  components (or partially assembled kits), and you move a whole bag from one crate/box to another, a true \u001b[1mself-\u001b[m\r\n  \u001b[1mreferential hierarchy (\u001b[94;22mparent_location_id\u001b[39;1m)\u001b[m means moving one bag updates the location path of every component and\r\n  sub-bag inside it in a single operation.\r\n\n  Let's sharpen that into a domain concept (\u001b[1mStorage Location\u001b[m) and check how \u001b[1mComponent\u001b[m quantities interact with it:\u001b[?7l\r\n\n\u001b[K  ❓ \u001b[1mQ5\u001b[m - \u001b[1mHierarchical Storage Locations & Moving Bags\u001b[m: If we model \u001b[1mStorage Location\u001b[m as a self-referential tree (\u001b[94mid\u001b[m,\u001b[?7h\u001b[117G\r\n  \u001b[94mname\u001b[m, \u001b[94mkind\u001b[m such as \u001b[94mCrate\u001b[m / \u001b[94mBox\u001b[m / \u001b[94mBinder\u001b[m / \u001b[94mBag\u001b[m / \u001b[94mDrawer\u001b[m, \u001b[94mparent_id\u001b[m, \u001b[94mnotes\u001b[m)—for example, \u001b[94mCrate 1 > Audio IC Bag > Bag\u001b[m\r\n  \u001b[94m#4\u001b[m—so you can reparent any \u001b[94mStorage Location\u001b[m "]
[0.000, "o", "(and everything nested inside it moves automatically):\r\n\n  Can the \u001b[1msame Component\u001b[m exist in \u001b[1mmultiple Storage Locations at once\u001b[m (e.g., 20x \u001b[94mTL072\u001b[m in \u001b[94mCrate 1 > Bulk Bag\u001b[m AND 5x\r\n  \u001b[94mTL072\u001b[m in \u001b[94mPedal Box B > Active Parts Bag\u001b[m), OR does each \u001b[1mComponent\u001b[m record point to \u001b[1mone\u001b[m \u001b[94mStorage Location\u001b[m (the specific\r\n  inner bag/drawer where that stash lives)?\r\n\n  • \u001b[1mOption A — One \u001b[94;22mStorage Location\u001b[39;1m per \u001b[94;22mComponent\u001b[39;1m record\u001b[m: Every \u001b[94mComponent\u001b[m points to a single leaf (or intermediate)\r\n  \u001b[94mSto\u001b[m\r\n⡿  \u001b[90mLoadin\u001b[94mg...\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[90m└ Tip: Press ctrl+g to open an external editor for long prompts.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[90m────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────"]
