[0.050, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\u001b[29ACan the \u001b[1msame Component\u001b[m exist in \u001b[1mmultiple Storage Locations at once\u001b[m (e.g., 20x \u001b[94mTL072\u001b[m in \u001b[94mCrate 1 > Bulk Bag\u001b[m AND 5x\r\n  \u001b[94mTL072\u001b[m in \u001b[94mPedal Box B > Active Parts Bag\u001b[m), OR does each \u001b[1mComponent\u001b[m record point to \u001b[1mone\u001b[m \u001b[94mStorage Location\u001b[m (the specific\r\n  inner bag/drawer where that stash lives)?\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\n  • \u001b[1mOption A — One \u001b[94;22mStorage Location\u001b[39;1m per \u001b[94;22mComponent\u001b[39;1m record\u001b[m: Every \u001b[94mComponent\u001b[m points to a single leaf (or intermediate)\r\n  \u001b[94mStorage Location\u001b[m (\u001b[94mlocation_id\u001b[m). If you move that bag to another crate/box, the \u001b[94mStorage Location\u001b[m's \u001b[94mparent_id\u001b[m changes\r\n  and the breadcrumb (\u001b[94mCrate 2 > Bag A\u001b[m) updates everywhere. If you ever keep a separate stash in a Kit Build's box,\u001b[K\r\n  that's handled by allocating parts to the \u001b[1mKit Build\u001b[m (which can also have its own \u001b[94mStorage Location\u001b[m, e.g., \u001b[94mBox: Klon\u001b[m\r\n  \u001b[94mClone WIP\u001b[m).\u001b[K\r\n  • \u001b[1mOption B — Stock Lots / Inventory B"]
[0.000, "o", "alances per Location\u001b[m: A single catalog \u001b[94mComponent\u001b[m has multiple \u001b[94mInventory Lot\u001b[m /\r\n  location rows, each with its own \u001b[94mlocation_id\u001b[m and \u001b[94mquantity\u001b[m. Moving a bag still reparents the \u001b[94mStorage Location\u001b[m, and\u001b[K\r\n  you can split a component's stock across multiple bags/boxes, at the cost of choosing which location when\u001b[K\r\n  adding/consuming stock (defaulting to the primary location when there's only one).\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\u001b[?7l\n\u001b[K  ➡️ \u001b[1mRecommended\u001b[m: \u001b[1mOption A\u001b[m (each \u001b[1mComponent\u001b[m has one \u001b[94mlocation_id\u001b[m in the hierarchical \u001b[1mStorage Location\u001b[m tree, AND each\u001b[?7h\u001b[115G\u001b[?7l\r\n\u001b[K  \u001b[1mKit Build\u001b[m can also be assigned a \u001b[94mlocation_id\u001b[m in that same tree for \"partially assembled kit boxes\"), unless you\u001b[?7h\u001b[114G\r\n  regularly keep unallocated loose stock of the exact same component split across multiple unrelated bags. Which fits\r\n  your workflow better: \u001b[1mOption A\u001b[m (one location per Component + locations on Kit Builds) or \u001b[1mOption B\u001b[m (multiple\u001b[K\r\n  loca"]
