[0.018, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\r\n\n\n\u001b[?5W\u001b[31A  That is the most honest description of a hobbyist electronics bench ever—ordering a second or third bag from\r\n  Tayda/Mouser because you couldn't find the first one!\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\n  That means \u001b[1mOption B\u001b[m is essential: a single logical \u001b[1mComponent\u001b[m in the catalog (e.g., \u001b[94m10kΩ 1% 1/4W Metal Film Resistor\u001b[m\r\n  or \u001b[94mTL072IP DIP-8\u001b[m) can have \u001b[1mmultiple physical stashes\u001b[m across different \u001b[1mStorage Locations\u001b[m (e.g., 85 in \u001b[94mCrate 1 >\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n  \u001b[94mMouser Order Bag 2024 > Bag 12\u001b[m and 40 in \u001b[94mBox B > Resistor Bag\u001b[m), and a \u001b[1mKit Build\u001b[m itself can also live in a \u001b[1mStorage\u001b[m\r\n  \u001b[1mLocation\u001b[m (e.g., \u001b[94mCrate 2 > Fuzz Face WIP Box\u001b[m).\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\n  Let's sharpen the domain language for this right now before we update \u001b[34;4m\u001b]8;id=jk74c850d0a5d596b;file:///Users/brett/Demos/audio-inventory-experiment/audio_inventory_skilled/GLOSSARY.md\u0007GLOSSARY.md\u001b[m\u001b]8;;\u0007:\r\n\u001b[K\n  • \u001b[1mComponent\u001b[m: The distinct catalog definition of a part (its category, original spec st"]
[0.000, "o", "ring, canonicalized\r\n  electrical/parametric specs, package, and general notes). Its total quantity on hand is the sum of its \u001b[1mStock Lots\u001b[m.\r\n  • \u001b[1mStorage Location\u001b[m: A physical container or sub-container in a nesting hierarchy (\u001b[94mparent_id\u001b[m), such as a \u001b[94mCrate\u001b[m, \u001b[94mBox\u001b[m,\r\n  \u001b[94mBinder\u001b[m, \u001b[94mDrawer\u001b[m, or \u001b[94mBag\u001b[m, which can hold child \u001b[1mStorage Locations\u001b[m, \u001b[1mStock Lots\u001b[m, and \u001b[1mKit Builds\u001b[m, and can be moved\u001b[K\r\n  (reparented) as a unit.\u001b[K\r\n  • \u001b[1mStock Lot\u001b[m (or \u001b[1mStash\u001b[m): A physical quantity of a specific \u001b[1mComponent\u001b[m stored at a specific \u001b[1mStorage Location\u001b[m\r\n  (optionally with lot-specific info like supplier/order reference or bag label, e.g., when you bought a second bag\r\n  from Mouser).\u001b[K\r\n  ──────\u001b[K\u001b[?7l\r\n\u001b[K  ❓ \u001b[1mQ6\u001b[m - \u001b[1mDomain Term & Lot Metadata (\"Stock Lot\" vs \"Stash\")\u001b[m: When you have two separate bags of the same \u001b[1mComponent\u001b[?7h\u001b[117G\u001b[?7l\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[K  in different \u001b[1mStorage Locations\u001b[m, what should we call each ph"]
[0.000, "o", "ysical pile in our domain language, and what per-pile\u001b[?7h\u001b[115G\r\n  metadata (beyond \u001b[94mcomponent_id\u001b[m, \u001b[94mlocation_id\u001b[m, and \u001b[94mquantity\u001b[m) is useful to track on it?\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\n  For example, when you toss a new Mouser/Tayda bag into a crate, the bag itself often has a supplier part number,\r\n  order date/note, or even measured batch notes (like a bag of transistors from a specific vendor):\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\n  • ``\u001b[K\r\n⣟  \u001b[90mWorking.\u001b[94m..\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[90m────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[94m>\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[90m────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────"]
