[0.017, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\u001b[29ALet's sharpen the domain language for this right now before we update \u001b[34;4m\u001b]8;id=jk2022bee300dc73aa;file:///Users/brett/Demos/audio-inventory-experiment/audio_inventory_skilled/GLOSSARY.md\u0007GLOSSARY.md\u001b[m\u001b]8;;\u0007:\r\n\u001b[K\n  • \u001b[1mComponent\u001b[m: The distinct catalog definition of a part (its category, original spec string, canonicalized\r\n  electrical/parametric specs, package, and general notes). Its total quantity on hand is the sum of its \u001b[1mStock Lots\u001b[m.\r\n  • \u001b[1mStorage Location\u001b[m: A physical container or sub-container in a nesting hierarchy (\u001b[94mparent_id\u001b[m), such as a \u001b[94mCrate\u001b[m, \u001b[94mBox\u001b[m,\r\n  \u001b[94mBinder\u001b[m, \u001b[94mDrawer\u001b[m, or \u001b[94mBag\u001b[m, which can hold child \u001b[1mStorage Locations\u001b[m, \u001b[1mStock Lots\u001b[m, and \u001b[1mKit Builds\u001b[m, and can be moved\u001b[K\r\n  (reparented) as a unit.\u001b[K\r\n  • \u001b[1mStock Lot\u001b[m (or \u001b[1mStash\u001b[m): A physical quantity of a specific \u001b[1mComponent\u001b[m stored at a specific \u001b[1mStorage Location\u001b[m\r\n  (optionally with lot-specific info like supplier/order reference o"]
[0.000, "o", "r bag label, e.g., when you bought a second bag\r\n  from Mouser).\u001b[K\r\n  ──────\u001b[K\u001b[?7l\r\n\u001b[K  ❓ \u001b[1mQ6\u001b[m - \u001b[1mDomain Term & Lot Metadata (\"Stock Lot\" vs \"Stash\")\u001b[m: When you have two separate bags of the same \u001b[1mComponent\u001b[?7h\u001b[117G\u001b[?7l\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[K  in different \u001b[1mStorage Locations\u001b[m, what should we call each physical pile in our domain language, and what per-pile\u001b[?7h\u001b[115G\r\n  metadata (beyond \u001b[94mcomponent_id\u001b[m, \u001b[94mlocation_id\u001b[m, and \u001b[94mquantity\u001b[m) is useful to track on it?\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\n  For example, when you toss a new Mouser/Tayda bag into a crate, the bag itself often has a supplier part number,\r\n  order date/note, or even measured batch notes (like a bag of transistors from a specific vendor):\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\n  • \u001b[94mcomponent_id\u001b[m (the catalog \u001b[1mComponent\u001b[m)\n\u001b[36D\u001b[94mlocation_id\u001b[m (the \u001b[1mStorage Location\u001b[m in the hierarchy, e.g., \u001b[94mCrate 1 > Big Bag B > Small Bag 4\u001b[m)\n\u001b[92D\u001b[94mquantity\u001b[m (integer count in this specific bag/location)\u001b[K\n\u001b[54D\u001b[94msupplier\u001b[m & \u001b[94msupplier"]
[0.000, "o", "_part_no\u001b[m (optional, since one bag might have come from Tayda and another from Mouser)\r\n\u001b[4C\u001b[94mlot_notes\u001b[m (optional freeform note, e.g., \u001b[94m\"Tayda 2025 order\"\u001b[m or \u001b[94m\"loose strip\"\u001b[m)\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\n  And for ergonomics: if a \u001b[1mComponent\u001b[m only has \u001b[1mone\u001b[m Stock Lot (the 80% case once organized), the UI can let you \u001b[94m+1 / -1\u001b[m\r\n  its quantity directly inline without an extra modal; if it has \u001b[1mmultiple\u001b[m Stock Lots, the UI shows the breakdown by\u001b[K\r\n  locat\u001b[K\r\n⢿ \n\n\u001b[?2026l"]
