[0.050, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\u001b[?25l\u001b[0 q\r\u001b[29A\u001b[90m────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[37;1m/Users/brett/Demos/audio-inventory-experiment/audio_inventory_skilled/GLOSSARY.md\u001b[m  \u001b[32m+10\u001b[m \u001b[31m-2\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[37m  \u001b[90m 1 \u001b[m    **Component**:\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[37m  \u001b[90m 2 \u001b[39;48;2;53;13;14m \u001b[31m-  \u001b[39mA distinct electronic part or hardware item in the catalog defined by its category and structured parametric\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[4C\u001b[37m\u001b[1K \u001b[48;2;53;13;14m \u001b[31m   \u001b[39mattributes (e.g., a \u001b[38;2;151;198;123m`10kΩ 1% 1/4W Metal Film Through-Hole Resistor`\u001b[39m or a \u001b[38;2;151;198;123m`TL072IP DIP-8 Op-Amp`\u001b[39m), along with\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[4C\u001b[37m\u001b[1K \u001b[48;2;53;13;14m \u001b[31m   \u001b[39mits quantity on hand and physical storage location"]
[0.000, "o", ".\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[37m  \u001b[90m 2 \u001b[39;48;2;14;52;15m \u001b[32m+  \u001b[39mA distinct electronic part, sub-assembly, or hardware specification in the catalog defined by its category,\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[4C\u001b[37m\u001b[1K \u001b[48;2;14;52;15m \u001b[32m   \u001b[39moriginal spec string, and structured parametric attributes (e.g., a \u001b[38;2;151;198;123m`10kΩ 1% 1/4W Metal Film Through-Hole\u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[4C\u001b[37m\u001b[1K \u001b[48;2;14;52;15m \u001b[32m   \u001b[38;2;151;198;123mResistor`\u001b[39m, a \u001b[38;2;151;198;123m`TL072IP DIP-8 Op-Amp`\u001b[39m, or a \u001b[38;2;151;198;123m`Daisy Seed MCU Board`\u001b[39m), whose total quantity on hand is the sum of\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[4C\u001b[37m\u001b[1K \u001b[48;2;14;52;15m \u001b[32m   \u001b[39mits **Stock Lots**.\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[37m  \u001b[90m 3 \u001b[m    _Avoid_: Item, SKU, Product, Material\r\n\u001b[37m  \u001b[90m 4 \u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[37m  \u001b[90m 5 \u001b[39;48;2;14;52;15m \u001b[32m+  \u001b[39m**Storage Location**:\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[37m  \u001b[90m 6 \u001b[39;48;2;14;52;15m \u001b[32m+  \u001b[39mA physical container or sub-container in a self-referential nesting hierarchy (e.g., a \u001b[38;2;151;198;123m`Crate`\u001b[39m containing a\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[4C\u001b[37m\u001b[1K \u001b[48;2;14"]
[0.000, "o", ";52;15m \u001b[32m   \u001b[38;2;151;198;123m`Bag`\u001b[39m containing a smaller \u001b[38;2;151;198;123m`Bag`\u001b[39m, \u001b[38;2;151;198;123m`Box`\u001b[39m, \u001b[38;2;151;198;123m`Binder`\u001b[39m, or \u001b[38;2;151;198;123m`Drawer`\u001b[39m) that holds child **Storage Locations**, **Stock\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[4C\u001b[37m\u001b[1K \u001b[48;2;14;52;15m \u001b[32m   \u001b[39mLots**, or **Kit Builds** and can be moved as a unit.\u001b[K\u001b[?7l\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[K\u001b[37m  \u001b[90m 7 \u001b[39;48;2;14;52;15m \u001b[32m+  \u001b[39m_Avoid_: Bin, Warehouse, Shelf, Slot                                                                           \u001b[?7h\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[37m  \u001b[90m 8 \u001b[39;48;2;14;52;15m \u001b[32m+  \u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[37m  \u001b[90m 9 \u001b[39;48;2;14;52;15m \u001b[32m+  \u001b[39m**Stock Lot**:\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[37m  \u001b[90m10 \u001b[39;48;2;14;52;15m \u001b[32m+  \u001b[39mA physical quantity of a specific **Component** stored at a single **Storage Location**, optionally carrying\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[4C\u001b[37m\u001b[1K \u001b[48;2;14;52;15m \u001b[32m   \u001b[39mlot-specific supplier details or notes (such as when duplicate bags of the same part live in different\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[4C\u001b[37m\u001b[1K \u001b[48;2;14;52;15m \u001b[32m   \u001b[39mco"]
[0.000, "o", "ntainers).\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[90m  … 6 more lines (f for full diff)\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[K\n  \u001b[94;1mshift+tab\u001b[90;22m to auto-approve file edits\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[1mAccept this file edit?\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[94m> 1. Yes, accept this change\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n  2. No, reject this change\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\n  \u001b[94;1m↑/↓\u001b[90;22m Navigate · \u001b[94;1mtab\u001b[90;22m Amend · \u001b[94;1mf\u001b[90;22m full diff\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[?2026l"]
[11.059, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\u001b[0 q\r\u001b[30A  in different \u001b[1mStorage Locations\u001b[m, what should we call each physical pile in our domain language, and what per-pile\u001b[K\r\n  metadata (beyond \u001b[94mcomponent_id\u001b[m, \u001b[94mlocation_id\u001b[m, and \u001b[94mquantity\u001b[m) is useful to track on it?\r\n\u001b[K\n  For example, when you toss a new Mouser/Tayda bag into a crate, the bag itself often has a supplier part number,\r\n  order date/note, or even measured batch notes (like a bag of transistors from a specific vendor):\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\n  • \u001b[94mcomponent_id\u001b[m (the catalog \u001b[1mComponent\u001b[m)\u001b[K\r\n  • \u001b[94mlocation_id\u001b[m (the \u001b[1mStorage Location\u001b[m in the hierarchy, e.g., \u001b[94mCrate 1 > Big Bag B > Small Bag 4\u001b[m)\u001b[K\r\n  • \u001b[94mquantity\u001b[m (integer count in this specific bag/location)\u001b[K\r\n  • \u001b[94msupplier\u001b[m & \u001b[94msupplier_part_no\u001b[m (optional, since one bag might have come from Tayda and another from Mouser)\u001b[K\r\n  • \u001b[94mlot_notes\u001b[m (optional freeform note, e.g., \u001b[94m\"Tayda 2025 order\"\u001b[m or \u001b[94m\"loose strip\"\u001b[m)\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\n  And for ergonomics: if a \u001b[1mC"]
[0.000, "o", "omponent\u001b[m only has \u001b[1mone\u001b[m Stock Lot (the 80% case once organized), the UI can let you \u001b[94m+1 / -1\u001b[m\r\n  its quantity directly inline without an extra modal; if it has \u001b[1mmultiple\u001b[m Stock Lots, the UI shows the breakdown by\u001b[K\r\n  location path (e.g., \u001b[94mTotal: 125 (85 in Crate 1 > Bag A, 40 in Box 2)\u001b[m) and lets you pick which lot to decrement (or\u001b[K\r\n  merge two lots when you physically combine the bags!).\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\u001b[?7l\n\u001b[K  ➡️ \u001b[1mRecommended\u001b[m: Name this concept \u001b[1mStock Lot\u001b[m in \u001b[94mGLOSSARY.md\u001b[m (with \u001b[94mcomponent_id\u001b[m, \u001b[94mlocation_id\u001b[m, \u001b[94mquantity\u001b[m, optional\u001b[?7h\u001b[113G\r\n  \u001b[94msupplier\u001b[m/\u001b[94msupplier_part_no\u001b[m, and \u001b[94mlot_notes\u001b[m, plus a one-click \u001b[1m\"Merge Lots\"\u001b[m action when you physically combine\u001b[K\r\n  duplicate bags into one location). Does \u001b[1mStock Lot\u001b[m and this field/UX model feel right?\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[90m─────────────────────────────────────────────────────"]
