[0.018, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\r\u001b[29A\u001b[32m●\u001b[m \u001b[33;1mExplored\u001b[m 1 file \u001b[37m(01-component-category-taxonomy-and-parametric-schema.md)\u001b[m\n\u001b[72D\u001b[33;1mdited\u001b[m 1 file \u001b[37m(02-bom-matching-stock-allocation-and-build-lifecycle.md)\u001b[m \u001b[37m(ctrl+o to expand)\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[K\n  I have claimed the next frontier ticket on the \u001b[34;4m\u001b]8;id=jk47dfc3218110f814;file:///Users/brett/Demos/audio-inventory-experiment/audio_inventory_skilled/.scratch/audio-inventory/map.md\u0007map\u001b[m\u001b]8;;\u0007: **\u001b[34;4m\u001b]8;id=jkf97e0d8b0ec707e7;file:///Users/brett/Demos/audio-inventory-experiment/audio_inventory_skilled/.scratch/audio-inventory/issues/02-bom-matching-stock-allocation-and-build-lifecycle.md\u0007BOM Matching, Stock Allocation, and Build Lifecycle\u001b[m\u001b]8;;\u0007**.\r\n\u001b[K\n  Let's work through the decisions for this ticket one question at a time.\r\n  ──────\u001b[K\u001b[?7l\r\n\u001b[K  ❓ \u001b[1mQ1\u001b[m - \u001b[1mBOM Line Component Linking & Partial Kits\u001b[m: When adding or importing a \u001b[1mBOM Line\u001b[m onto a \u001b[1mKit Build\u001b[m (e.g., \u001b[94mR1,\u001b[?7h\u001b[117G\u001b[?7l\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[K  \u001b[94mR2, R5: 4k7 1% 1"]
[0.000, "o", "/4W Metal Film\u001b[m, qty 3), how should that \u001b[1mBOM Line\u001b[m link to your \u001b[1mComponent\u001b[m catalog and handle parts\u001b[?7h\u001b[115G\r\n  that came pre-packaged in a partial kit?\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\n  1. \u001b[1m(Recommended) Dual Spec + Optional Component Link with \"Included in Kit\" Fulfillment Source\u001b[m:\r\n      • Every \u001b[1mBOM Line\u001b[m stores its own required specification (\u001b[94mraw_spec_text\u001b[m, \u001b[94mcategory\u001b[m, normalized value/attributes,\r\n\u001b[6C\u001b[94mquantity_required\u001b[m, \u001b[94mreference_designators\u001b[m, \u001b[94mnotes\u001b[m) \u001b[3mplus\u001b[m an optional foreign key (\u001b[94mcomponent_id\u001b[m) to a catalog\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[6C\u001b[1mComponent\u001b[m.\u001b[K\n\u001b[10D• \u001b[1mAuto-match & Parametric Candidates\u001b[m: When a \u001b[1mBOM Line\u001b[m is created or imported, the app parses its spec and\r\n\u001b[6Cautomatically links \u001b[94mcomponent_id\u001b[m if there is a single exact parametric match in your catalog. If multiple\r\n\u001b[6Ccatalog \u001b[1mComponents\u001b[m satisfy the spec (e.g., you have both Royal Ohm and Vishay \u001b[94m4.7kΩ 1% 1/4W\u001b[m resistors, or both\r\n\u001b[6C50V and 100V \u001b[94m47nF\u001b[m film caps) o"]
[0.000, "o", "r if none exists yet, the line remains \u001b[94mUnlinked\u001b[m and the UI shows matching catalog\r\n\u001b[6Ccandidates (or a 1-click \"Create Component from BOM Line\" action) for you to pick.\u001b[K\n\u001b[82D• \u001b[1mPartial Kit Support\u001b[m: A \u001b[1mBOM Line\u001b[m can be marked as \u001b[1mIncluded in Kit\u001b[m (for partial kits where the PCB, enclosure,\r\n\u001b[6Cor specialized IC came in the kit box, while you supply standard passives from your stash), which marks the\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[6Cline ready without deducting from your general catalog \u001b[1mStock Lots\u001b[m.\u001b[K\r\n  2. \u001b[1mStrict Foreign Key Only\u001b[m: Every \u001b[1mBOM Line\u001b[m must immediately point to a \u001b[94mcomponent_id\u001b[m in the \u001b[94mcomponents\u001b[m table (auto-\r\n  creating placeholder catalog components on BOM import even for parts you don't own or one-off kit parts).\u001b[K\r\n  3.\u001b[K\n\u001b[7C\u001b[90m.\u001b[94m.\u001b[m\n\n\n\u001b[11D\u001b[?2026l"]
