[0.017, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\u001b[29A1. \u001b[1m(Recommended) Dual Spec + Optional Component Link with \"Included in Kit\" Fulfillment Source\u001b[m:\r\n      • Every \u001b[1mBOM Line\u001b[m stores its own required specification (\u001b[94mraw_spec_text\u001b[m, \u001b[94mcategory\u001b[m, normalized value/attributes,\r\n\u001b[6C\u001b[94mquantity_required\u001b[m, \u001b[94mreference_designators\u001b[m, \u001b[94mnotes\u001b[m) \u001b[3mplus\u001b[m an optional foreign key (\u001b[94mcomponent_id\u001b[m) to a catalog\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[6C\u001b[1mComponent\u001b[m.\u001b[K\n\u001b[10D• \u001b[1mAuto-match & Parametric Candidates\u001b[m: When a \u001b[1mBOM Line\u001b[m is created or imported, the app parses its spec and\r\n\u001b[6Cautomatically links \u001b[94mcomponent_id\u001b[m if there is a single exact parametric match in your catalog. If multiple\r\n\u001b[6Ccatalog \u001b[1mComponents\u001b[m satisfy the spec (e.g., you have both Royal Ohm and Vishay \u001b[94m4.7kΩ 1% 1/4W\u001b[m resistors, or both\r\n\u001b[6C50V and 100V \u001b[94m47nF\u001b[m film caps) or if none exists yet, the line remains \u001b[94mUnlinked\u001b[m and the UI shows matching catalog\r\n\u001b[6Ccandidates (or a 1-click \"Create Component from BOM Line\" action) for y"]
[0.000, "o", "ou to pick.\u001b[K\n\u001b[82D• \u001b[1mPartial Kit Support\u001b[m: A \u001b[1mBOM Line\u001b[m can be marked as \u001b[1mIncluded in Kit\u001b[m (for partial kits where the PCB, enclosure,\r\n\u001b[6Cor specialized IC came in the kit box, while you supply standard passives from your stash), which marks the\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[6Cline ready without deducting from your general catalog \u001b[1mStock Lots\u001b[m.\u001b[K\r\n  2. \u001b[1mStrict Foreign Key Only\u001b[m: Every \u001b[1mBOM Line\u001b[m must immediately point to a \u001b[94mcomponent_id\u001b[m in the \u001b[94mcomponents\u001b[m table (auto-\r\n  creating placeholder catalog components on BOM import even for parts you don't own or one-off kit parts).\u001b[K\r\n  3. \u001b[1mPure Parametric Query Only\u001b[m: \u001b[1mBOM Lines\u001b[m never link to a specific \u001b[94mcomponent_id\u001b[m until you physically consume stock\r\n  during the build.\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\u001b[?7l\n\u001b[K  ➡️ \u001b[1mOption 1 (Dual Spec + Optional \u001b[94;22mcomponent_id\u001b[39;1m Link with \"Included in Kit\" support)\u001b[m—this lets you import a full BOM\u001b[?7h\u001b[118G\u001b[?7l\r\n\u001b[K  immediately without polluting your catalog with unvetted duplicates,"]
[0.000, "o", " supports choosing between compatible parts in\u001b[?7h\u001b[117G\r\n  your stash, and cleanly handles partial kits. Does this fit how you work?\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[90m────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[34;1m> sgtm\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\u001b[?7l\n\u001b[K  ❓ \u001b[1mQ2\u001b[m - \u001b[1mStock Allocation, Picking into a Project Box, and Consumption across Stock Lots\u001b[m: In [Component Category\u001b[?7h\u001b[114G\u001b[?7l\r\n\u001b[K  Taxonomy & Parametric Schema](file:///Users/brett/Demos/audio-inventory-\u001b[?7h\u001b[75G\r\n  experiment/audio_inventory_skilled/.scratch/audio-inventory/issues/01-compo\u001b[K\n\n\n\u001b[75D\u001b[?2026l"]
