[0.017, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\r\u001b[29A  ➡️ \u001b[1mOption 1 (Dual Spec + Optional \u001b[m\u001b[94mcomponent_id\u001b[m\u001b[1m Link with \"Included in Kit\" support)\u001b[m—this lets you import a full BOM\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[?5W\u001b[J  immediately without polluting your catalog with unvetted duplicates, supports choosing between compatible parts in\r\n  your stash, and cleanly handles partial kits. Does this fit how you work?\r\n\n\u001b[90m────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[34;1m> sgtm\u001b[?7l\u001b[m\r\n\n\u001b[K  ❓ \u001b[1mQ2\u001b[m - \u001b[1mStock Allocation, Picking into a Project Box, and Consumption across Stock Lots\u001b[m: In\u001b[?7h\u001b[94G\r\n  \u001b[34;4m\u001b]8;id=jk99bee5b783ea10ce;file:///Users/brett/Demos/audio-inventory-experiment/audio_inventory_skilled/.scratch/audio-inventory/issues/01-component-category-taxonomy-and-parametric-schema.md\u0007Component Category Taxonomy & Parametric Schema\u001b[m\u001b]8;;\u0007, we established that a \u001b[1mComponent\u001b[m can have multiple \u001b[1m"]
[0.000, "o", "Stock Lots\u001b[m\r\n  across different \u001b[1mStorage Locations\u001b[m, and a \u001b[1mKit Build\u001b[m can itself live in a physical \u001b[1mStorage Location\u001b[m (like a project\r\n  box or bag).\r\n\n  How should reserving, picking/kitting, and consuming parts work between a \u001b[1mBOM Line\u001b[m and your \u001b[1mStock Lots\u001b[m?\r\n\n  1. \u001b[1m(Recommended) Three-State BOM Line Fulfillment (\u001b[94;22mUnallocated\u001b[39;1m → \u001b[94;22mAllocated / Kitted\u001b[39;1m → \u001b[94;22mInstalled\u001b[39;1m + \u001b[94;22mIncluded in Kit\u001b[39;1m)\u001b[m:\r\n\u001b[6C• \u001b[1mUnallocated (Planning / Readiness Check)\u001b[m: The \u001b[1mBOM Line\u001b[m links to a \u001b[94mcomponent_id\u001b[m (or shows parametric candidate\r\n\u001b[6Cstock). Readiness compare checks \u001b[94mquantity_required\u001b[m against \u001b[1mAvailable Stock\u001b[m (\u001b[94mTotal On Hand across Stock Lots −\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[6C\u001b[94mTotal Soft-Reserved by other builds\u001b[m).\n\u001b[37D• \u001b[1mAllocated (Soft-Reserved vs. Physically Kitted)\u001b[m:\r\n\t  • \u001b[1mSoft-Reserved (\u001b[94;22mReserved\u001b[39;1m in place)\u001b[m: Marks the quantity reserved for this \u001b[1mKit Build\u001b[m (optionally pinned to a\r\n\t"]
[0.000, "o", "  specific \u001b[1mStock Lot\u001b[m, or against the \u001b[1mComponent\u001b[m generally) without moving the parts yet; reduces \u001b[3mAvailable\u001b[m\r\n\t  \u001b[3mStock\u001b[m for other builds while leaving physical \u001b[1mStock Lot\u001b[m counts untouched so your drawer counts still match\r\n\t  reality.\n\u001b[8D• \u001b[1mPhysically Kitted / Picked (\u001b[94;22mPicked\u001b[39;1m into the Kit Build's box)\u001b[m: When you pull parts from a drawer/binder\r\n\t  and drop them into the \u001b[1mKit Build\u001b[m's project box/bag, the app deducts \u001b[94mquantity\u001b[m from the source \u001b[1mStock Lot\u001b[m and\r\n\t  records the\r\n\n\n⣽  \u001b[90mWorking...\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[90m────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[94m>\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[90m─────────────────────"]
