[0.017, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\u001b[29AHow should reserving, picking/kitting, and consuming parts work between a \u001b[1mBOM Line\u001b[m and your \u001b[1mStock Lots\u001b[m?\r\n\u001b[K\n  1. \u001b[1m(Recommended) Three-State BOM Line Fulfillment (\u001b[94;22mUnallocated\u001b[39;1m → \u001b[94;22mAllocated / Kitted\u001b[39;1m → \u001b[94;22mInstalled\u001b[39;1m + \u001b[94;22mIncluded in Kit\u001b[39;1m)\u001b[m:\r\n      • \u001b[1mUnallocated (Planning / Readiness Check)\u001b[m: The \u001b[1mBOM Line\u001b[m links to a \u001b[94mcomponent_id\u001b[m (or shows parametric candidate\r\n\u001b[6Cstock). Readiness compare checks \u001b[94mquantity_required\u001b[m against \u001b[1mAvailable Stock\u001b[m (\u001b[94mTotal On Hand across Stock Lots −\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[6C\u001b[94mTotal Soft-Reserved by other builds\u001b[m).\u001b[K\n\u001b[37D• \u001b[1mAllocated (Soft-Reserved vs. Physically Kitted)\u001b[m:\n\u001b[50D    • \u001b[1mSoft-Reserved (\u001b[94;22mReserved\u001b[39;1m in place)\u001b[m: Marks the quantity reserved for this \u001b[1mKit Build\u001b[m (optionally pinned to a\r\n\t  specific \u001b[1mStock Lot\u001b[m, or against the \u001b[1mComponent\u001b[m generally) without moving the parts yet; reduces \u001b[3mAvailable\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n\t  \u001b[3mStock\u001b"]
[0.000, "o", "[m for other builds while leaving physical \u001b[1mStock Lot\u001b[m counts untouched so your drawer counts still match\r\n\t  reality.\u001b[K\n\u001b[8D• \u001b[1mPhysically Kitted / Picked (\u001b[94;22mPicked\u001b[39;1m into the Kit Build's box)\u001b[m: When you pull parts from a drawer/binder\r\n\t  and drop them into the \u001b[1mKit Build\u001b[m's project box/bag, the app deducts \u001b[94mquantity\u001b[m from the source \u001b[1mStock Lot\u001b[m and\r\n\t  records the allocation on the \u001b[1mBOM Line\u001b[m (remembering \u001b[94msource_lot_id\u001b[m so if you cancel the build or un-kit the\r\n\t  part, 1 click returns it to its original \u001b[1mStock Lot\u001b[m).\u001b[K\n\u001b[56D• \u001b[1mInstalled / Consumed (\u001b[94;22mInstalled\u001b[39;1m on PCB)\u001b[m: When soldered/assembled onto the build during bench work, the \u001b[1mBOM\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[6C\u001b[1mLine\u001b[m transitions to \u001b[94mInstalled\u001b[m (if it wasn't already deducted at \u001b[94mPicked\u001b[m, it deducts from the chosen \u001b[1mStock Lot\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[6Cnow).\u001b[K\r\n  2. \u001b[1mImmediate Deduction Only (No Soft-Reserve / Kitting Distinction)\u001b[m: Allocating a part on a BOM immediately\r\n  decrements the"]
[0.000, "o", " \u001b[1mStock Lot\u001b[m quantity, with no distinction between \"reserved on paper\", \"bagged in the project box\",\r\n  and \"soldered to the PCB\".\u001b[K\r\n  3. \u001b[1mConsumption Only at Build Completion\u001b[m: Stock is never reserved or deducted per \u001b[1mBOM Line\u001b[m; the entire BOM is\r\n  deducted in one batch only when the whole \u001b[1mKit Build\u001b[m is marked \u001b[94mCompleted\u001b[m.\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\u001b[?7l\n\u001b[K  ➡️ \u001b[1mOption 1 (Three-State BOM Line Fulfillment supporting both Soft-Reservation in place and Physical Picking into\u001b[?7h\u001b[116G\u001b[?7l\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[K  \u001b[1mthe Kit Build box, plus Installed)\u001b[m—this ensures drawer counts match physical reality whether you pre-bag kits or\u001b[?7h\u001b[115G\r\n  pull parts straight fr\u001b[K\n\n\n\u001b[22D\u001b[?2026l"]
