[0.083, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\r\u001b[29A  ❓ \u001b[1mQ5\u001b[m - \u001b[1mCloning a Kit Build\u001b[m: In \u001b]8;id=jkd55d4b18152a8b48;file:///Users/brett/Demos/audio-inventory-experiment/audio_inventory_skilled/GLOSSARY.md#L19-L21\u001b\\\u001b[4;34;4mG\u001b[m\u001b[4;34;4mL\u001b[m\u001b[4;34;4mO\u001b[m\u001b[4;34;4mS\u001b[m\u001b[4;34;4mS\u001b[m\u001b[4;34;4mA\u001b[m\u001b[4;34;4mR\u001b[m\u001b[4;34;4mY\u001b[m\u001b[4;34;4m.\u001b[m\u001b[4;34;4mm\u001b[m\u001b[4;34;4md\u001b[m\u001b[4;34;4m:\u001b[m\u001b[4;34;4m1\u001b[m\u001b[4;34;4m9\u001b[m\u001b[4;34;4m-\u001b[m\u001b[4;34;4m2\u001b[m\u001b[4;34;4m1\u001b[m\u001b]8;;\u001b\\ and our \u001b]8;id=jka8fec6373ff6fa3a;file:///Users/brett/Demos/audio-inventory-experiment/audio_inventory_skilled/.scratch/audio-inventory/map.md#L28\u001b\\\u001b[4;34;4mm\u001b[m\u001b[4;34;4ma\u001b[m\u001b[4;34;4mp\u001b[m\u001b]8;;\u001b\\, we kept \u001b[1mKit Build\u001b[m as a single entity rather than\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[?5W\u001b[J  splitting into \"Project Template\" vs. \"Production Run\", with optional cloning if you ever build a second copy of a\r\n  pedal or synth module (e.g., building two DIY VCOs for a synth rack, or building a second overdrive pedal for a\r\n  friend).\r\n\n  When you click \u001b[1m\"Clone Kit Build\"\u001b[m on an existing \u001b[1mKit Build\u001b[m, what should be copied a"]
[0.000, "o", "nd what should be reset?\r\n\n  1. \u001b[1m(Recommended) Copy Spec, BOM Lines (with Component Links), and Reference Docs; Reset Status, Allocations, and\u001b[m\r\n  \u001b[1mBench Logs\u001b[m:\n\u001b[7D• \u001b[1mCopied\u001b[m: Build name (with \u001b[94m(Copy)\u001b[m or custom name prompt), category/type, description, external URLs,\r\n\u001b[6Cschematic/build-doc attachments (referencing the same PDFs without duplicating large files on disk), and all\r\n\u001b[6C\u001b[1mBOM Lines\u001b[m including their \u001b[94mraw_spec_text\u001b[m, \u001b[94mreference_designators\u001b[m, \u001b[94mquantity_required\u001b[m, linked \u001b[94mcomponent_id\u001b[m,\r\n\u001b[6C\u001b[94msubstitution_note\u001b[m, and whether a line is \u001b[94mIncluded in Kit\u001b[m.\n\u001b[57D• \u001b[1mReset\u001b[m: Status resets to \u001b[94mWishlist / Planned\u001b[m, \u001b[94mlocation_id\u001b[m is cleared (or prompted), every non-kit \u001b[1mBOM Line\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[6Cresets to \u001b[94mUnallocated\u001b[m (\u001b[94mquantity_allocated = 0\u001b[m, \u001b[94msource_lot_id = NULL\u001b[m), and \u001b[94mkit_log_entries\u001b[m / build photos start\r\n\u001b[6Cfresh.\r\n  2. \u001b[1mShallow Copy Only (BOM Spec Text Only)\u001b[m: Cloning copies only the raw BOM t"]
[0.001, "o", "ext without preserving any \u001b[94mcomponent_id\u001b[m\r\n  links or schematic PDF attachments.\u001b[?7l\r\n\n\u001b[K  ➡️ \u001b[1mOption 1 (Copy BOM Lines with their \u001b[94;22mcomponent_id\u001b[39;1m links and reference docs, while resetting status, stock\u001b[?7h\u001b[110G\u001b[m\r\n  \u001b[1mallocations, and bench logs)\u001b[m—so building a second unit reuses all your part-matching work immediately. Does this\r\n  complete our shared understanding for this ticket?\r\n\n\u001b[90m────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[34;1m> sgtm\u001b[m\r\n\n\u001b[32m●\u001b[m \u001b[33;1mExplored\u001b[m 1 file \u001b[37m(GLOSSARY-FORMAT.md)\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[33m●\u001b[m \u001b[33;1mEditing\u001b[m 1 file \u001b[37m(GLOSSARY.md)\u001b[m \u001b[37m(ctrl+o to expand)\u001b[m\r\n⣾  \u001b[90mReading file...\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[90m──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────"]
