[0.017, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\r\u001b[29A  ❓ \u001b[1mQ1\u001b[m - \u001b[1mComponent & Stock Lot CSV Import Workflow and Duplicate Reconciliation\u001b[m:\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[?5W\u001b[J  When importing \u001b[1mComponents\u001b[m and \u001b[1mStock Lots\u001b[m from a CSV file (such as a supplier order history export from Mouser,\r\n  DigiKey, Tayda, or LCSC, or a personal spreadsheet), how should column mapping and duplicate/near-match\r\n  reconciliation work?\r\n\n  Specifically, should the workflow operate as a \u001b[1mtwo-step staged import\u001b[m:\r\n\n  1. \u001b[1mUpload & Column Mapping\u001b[m: Upload a CSV (or paste tabular text), choose a default target \u001b[1mStorage Location\u001b[m (and\r\n  optional default supplier) for the batch, and map CSV columns (\u001b[94mraw_spec_text\u001b[m / Value, Category, Subtype,\r\n  Package/Footprint, Quantity, Storage Location path/name, Supplier, Supplier Part #, Datasheet URL, Notes) with\r\n  automatic header detection for common supplier exports and saved mapping presets.\r\n  2. \u001b[1mInteractive Staging & Reconciliation Preview\u001b[m: Before writing to the database, parse every row with the\r"]
[0.000, "o", "\n  deterministic spec parser and classify each row into one of three reconciliation states that the user can review or\r\n  override row-by-row (or in bulk):\n\u001b[29D• \u001b[1mExact Match\u001b[m (matches an existing \u001b[1mComponent\u001b[m by \u001b[94msupplier + supplier_part_no\u001b[m or by normalized category +\r\n\u001b[6Celectrical value + package + key attributes): Default action is \u001b[1mAdd / Increment Stock Lot\u001b[m on the existing\r\n\u001b[6C\u001b[1mComponent\u001b[m at the target \u001b[1mStorage Location\u001b[m (incrementing quantity if a lot at that location already exists, or\r\n\u001b[6Ccreating a new \u001b[1mStock Lot\u001b[m if placed in a different location).\n\u001b[60D• \u001b[1mNear / Ambiguous Match\u001b[m (e.g., same category and \u001b[94m4.7kΩ\u001b[m value, but the CSV omits wattage/tolerance or multiple\r\n\u001b[6Ccatalog \u001b[1mComponents\u001b[m match): Highlighted for review so you can pick which existing \u001b[1mComponent\u001b[m to add the \u001b[1mStock Lot\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[6Cto, or choose \u001b[1mCreate as New Component\u001b[m.\n\u001b[38D• \u001b[1mNo Match\u001b[m: Default action is \u001b[1mCreate New Component + Initial Stock Lot\u001b[m ("]
[0.000, "o", "auto-creating any new \u001b[1mStorage Location\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[6Cin the path if requested).\u001b[?7l\r\n\n\n\u001b[K  ➡️ \u001b[1mYes — use a two-step staged import (upload + column mapper with saved presets, followed by an interactive\u001b[?7h\u001b[111G\u001b[m\r\n  \u001b[1mreconciliation preview that auto-matches by supplier P/N or normalized parametric spec, defaults exact matches to\u001b[m\r\n  \u001b[1maddi\u001b[m\r\n⣟  \u001b[90mGenerating...\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[90m────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[94m>\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[90m──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────"]
