[0.067, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\r\u001b[29A\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[37m▸ Thought for 9s, 279 tokens\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\r\n  ❓ \u001b[1mQ2\u001b[m - \u001b[1mKit Build BOM CSV Import & Row Grouping Workflow\u001b[m:\u001b[K\r\n  When importing a \u001b[1mBOM\u001b[m into a \u001b[1mKit Build\u001b[m from a CSV or pasted table (such as an EDA export from KiCad/Eagle or a\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[?5W\u001b[J  PedalPCB/AionFX parts spreadsheet), how should row grouping, column mapping, and catalog matching work?\r\n\n  Specifically, should the \u001b[1mBOM\u001b[m import workflow support:\r\n\n  1. \u001b[1mFlexible Input & Column Mapping\u001b[m: Upload a CSV or paste clipboard rows, mapping columns to \u001b[94mraw_spec_text\u001b[m (Value /\r\n  Part Name), \u001b[94mreference_designators\u001b[m (e.g., \u001b[94mR1, R2, R5\u001b[m), \u001b[94mquantity_required\u001b[m (defaulting to count of designators or \u001b[94m1\u001b[m if\r\n  omitted), \u001b[94mcategory\u001b[m (inferred from reference designator prefix like \u001b[94mR\u001b[m, \u001b[94mC\u001b[m, \u001b[94mQ\u001b[m, \u001b[94mD\u001b[m, \u001b[94mU\u001b[m/\u001b[94mIC\u001b[m, \u001b[94mVR\u001b[m/\u001b[94mRV\u001b[m, \u001b[94mSW\u001b[m, \u001b[94mJ\u001b[m when not\r\n  explicitly mapped), \u001b[94mpackage_or_mounting\u001b[m, \u001b[94mnotes\u001b[m, and an optional \u001b["]
[0.000, "o", "94mIncluded in Kit\u001b[m flag.\r\n  2. \u001b[1mAutomatic Designator Grouping Toggle\u001b[m: EDA exports often list one reference designator per row (e.g., \u001b[94mR1 | 10k\u001b[m\r\n  and \u001b[94mR2 | 10k\u001b[m on separate lines). Provide an on-by-default \u001b[1m\"Combine rows with identical Category + Spec + Package\"\u001b[m\r\n  toggle during import that merges them into a single \u001b[1mBOM Line\u001b[m (\u001b[94mquantity_required = 2\u001b[m, \u001b[94mreference_designators = \"R1,\u001b[m\r\n  \u001b[94mR2\"\u001b[m).\r\n  3. \u001b[1mStaging Preview with Catalog Auto-Match\u001b[m: Before committing the import (with a choice to \u001b[1mAppend to\u001b[m or \u001b[1mReplace\u001b[m\r\n  existing unallocated \u001b[1mBOM Lines\u001b[m), display the parsed lines alongside their auto-matched catalog \u001b[1mComponent\u001b[m (if a\r\n  single exact parametric match exists), current \u001b[1mAvailable Stock\u001b[m, or candidate matches when ambiguous/unlinked.\u001b[?7l\r\n\n\u001b[K  ➡️ \u001b[1mYes — support CSV upload and clipboard paste with reference-designator prefix category inference (\u001b[94;22mR\u001b[39;1m→Resistors,\u001b[?7h\u001b[116G\u001b[m\r\n  \u001b[94mC\u001b[39;1m→Capaci"]
[0.000, "o", "tors, etc.), an on-by-default toggle to group identical spec rows into combined BOM Lines, and a staging\u001b[m\r\n  \u001b[1mpreview showing catalog auto-matches and Available Stock.\u001b[m\r\n\n\u001b[90m────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[34;1m> yes\u001b[m\r\n\n\u001b[37m▸ Thought for 15s\u001b[?7l\u001b[m\r\n\n\u001b[K  ❓ \u001b[1mQ3\u001b[m -\u001b[?7h\u001b[10G\r\n⣻  \u001b[90mThe problem involves correctly calculating component shortages across multiple kit builds, considering both alloca\u001b[94m...\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[90m└ Tip: Use /btw to ask a question without breaking context.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[90m───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────"]
