[0.016, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\r\u001b[29A\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[37m▸ Thought for 15s\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[?5W\u001b[J\u001b[?7l\n\u001b[K  ❓ \u001b[1mQ3\u001b[m - \u001b[1mMulti-Build Shopping List Aggregation & Shared Stock Deduction\u001b[m:\u001b[?7h\u001b[74G\r\n  When generating a shopping list across multiple \u001b[1mKit Builds\u001b[m (for example, all builds in \u001b[94mSourcing / Waiting on Parts\u001b[m\r\n  plus selected \u001b[94mWishlist / Planned\u001b[m builds), two builds may compete for the same unreserved \u001b[1mAvailable Stock\u001b[m—for\r\n  instance, Build A needs \u001b[94m4x TL072\u001b[m (\u001b[94mUnallocated\u001b[m), Build B needs \u001b[94m2x TL072\u001b[m (\u001b[94mUnallocated\u001b[m), and your \u001b[1mAvailable Stock\u001b[m is\r\n  \u001b[94m3x\u001b[m. Checking each build in isolation would falsely suggest you only need \u001b[94m1x\u001b[m instead of \u001b[94m3x\u001b[m.\r\n\n  How should the shopping list aggregator calculate net shortages and group lines across builds?\r\n\n  1. \u001b[1mAggregate Demand Before Deducting Available Stock\u001b[m:\n\u001b[49D• For each \u001b[1mBOM Line\u001b[m on the selected \u001b[1mKit Builds\u001b[m that is not yet fully fulfilled (\u001b[94mFulfillment Status\u001b[m in\r\n\u001b[6C\u001b[94mUnallocated\u001b[m, "]
[0.000, "o", "\u001b[94mReserved\u001b[m, \u001b[94mPicked\u001b[m, or \u001b[94mInstalled\u001b[m, excluding \u001b[94mIncluded in Kit\u001b[m), compute its remaining unallocated\r\n\u001b[6Cdemand: \u001b[94munallocated_needed = quantity_required - quantity_allocated\u001b[m.\n\u001b[68D• Group lines across all selected builds by linked \u001b[94mcomponent_id\u001b[m (or, for unlinked \u001b[1mBOM Lines\u001b[m where \u001b[94mcomponent_id\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[6C\u001b[94mIS NULL\u001b[m, group by normalized \u001b[94mcategory + canonical_value_display + package_or_mounting\u001b[m / \u001b[94mraw_spec_text\u001b[m).\r\n\u001b[6C• Calculate \u001b[1mNet Shortfall\u001b[m for each grouped part as:\n\n\n\u001b[53D\u001b[38;5;252mNet Shortfall = max(0, ∑ unallocated\\_needed - Available Stock)\u001b[m\n\n\u001b[63D\u001b[38;5;252m (where unlinked parts have `Available Stock = 0`).\u001b[m\r\n\n  2. \u001b[1mOptional Low-Stock Restock Toggle\u001b[m:\n\u001b[33D• Provide an optional \u001b[1m\"Include catalog low-stock restocking\"\u001b[m toggle that also pulls in any catalog \u001b[1mComponent\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[6Cwhose post-build remaining stock (\u001b[94mAvailable Stock - sum(unallocated_needed)\u001b[m) would sit below its\n\u001b[96D\u001b[94mlow_stock_threshol"]
