[0.018, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\r\u001b[29A\u001b[90m────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[34;1m> yes\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[37m▸ Thought for 13s\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[K\u001b[?7l\n\u001b[K  ❓ \u001b[1mQ4\u001b[m - \u001b[1mShopping List Overrides, Supplier Export Formats, and Receiving Parts\u001b[m:\u001b[?7h\u001b[81G\u001b[?7l\r\n\u001b[K  Once the aggregated shopping list is displayed, how should you adjust order quantities, export for specific\u001b[?7h\u001b[110G\r\n  suppliers, and record parts when an order arrives?\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\n  Specifically:\r\n\u001b[K\n  1. \u001b[1mLive Computed View with Inline Overrides\u001b[m: Rather than maintaining a separate stateful \"Purchase Order\" lifecycle,\r\n  the \u001b[1mShopping List\u001b[m is a live computed view over your selected \u001b[1mKit Builds\u001b[m (and optional low-stock restock filter).\u001b[K\r\n  Before exporting, each row lets you edit the \u001b[1mOrder Quantity\u001b[m (initialized to \u001b[1mNet Shortfall\u001b[m, so you can easily bump\r\n  \u001b[94m1x\u001b[m resistor up to \u001b[94m10x\u001b[m or \u001b["]
[0.000, "o", "94m50x\u001b[m for spares) and select/edit the target \u001b[94mSupplier\u001b[m and \u001b[94mSupplier Part #\u001b[m (pre-filled from\r\n  the linked \u001b[1mComponent\u001b[m's existing \u001b[1mStock Lot\u001b[m supplier metadata).\u001b[K\r\n  2. \u001b[1mExport Formats\u001b[m:\u001b[K\r\n      • \u001b[1mFull Shopping List CSV\u001b[m: Exports all columns (\u001b[94mCategory\u001b[m, \u001b[94mSpec / Component Name\u001b[m, \u001b[94mPackage\u001b[m, \u001b[94mSupplier\u001b[m, \u001b[94mSupplier\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[6C\u001b[94mPart #\u001b[m, \u001b[94mAvailable Stock\u001b[m, \u001b[94mNet Shortfall\u001b[m, \u001b[94mOrder Quantity\u001b[m, \u001b[94mKit Builds & Reference Designators\u001b[m, \u001b[94mNotes\u001b[m), optionally\r\n\u001b[6Cgrouped or filtered by \u001b[94mSupplier\u001b[m.\u001b[K\n\u001b[32D• \u001b[1mSupplier Quick-Order / Cart Format (CSV & Clipboard Copy)\u001b[m: Filters to a selected supplier (e.g., Mouser,\r\n\u001b[6CDigiKey, Tayda, LCSC) and formats \u001b[94mSupplier Part #, Order Quantity, Customer Reference (Kit Build names)\u001b[m for\r\n\u001b[6Cdirect paste or upload into supplier BOM/cart tools.\u001b[K\r\n  3. \u001b[1mClosing the Loop on Arrival\u001b[m: When parts arrive, you can either import the supplier's order CSV via the \u001b[1"]
[0.000, "o", "mComponent\u001b[m\r\n  \u001b[1m& Stock Lot CSV Import\u001b[m workflow (Q1), or use a \u001b[1m\"Receive Selected Lines into Stock\"\u001b[m action directly from the\u001b[K\r\n  shopping list to create/increment \u001b[1mStock Lots\u001b[m at a chosen \u001b[1mStorage Location\u001b[m (auto-creating and linking catalog\r\n  \u001b[1mComponents\u001b[m\u001b[K\n\n\n\u001b[10D\u001b[?2026l"]
