[0.066, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\u001b[?25l\u001b[0 q\u001b[29A\u001b[4C• \u001b[1mSupplier Quick-Order / Cart Format (CSV & Clipboard Copy)\u001b[m: Filters to a selected supplier (e.g., Mouser,\r\n      DigiKey, Tayda, LCSC) and formats \u001b[94mSupplier Part #, Order Quantity, Customer Reference (Kit Build names)\u001b[m for\u001b[K\r\n      direct paste or upload into supplier BOM/cart tools.\u001b[K\r\n  3. \u001b[1mClosing the Loop on Arrival\u001b[m: When parts arrive, you can either import the supplier's order CSV via the \u001b[1mComponent\u001b[m\r\n  \u001b[1m& Stock Lot CSV Import\u001b[m workflow (Q1), or use a \u001b[1m\"Receive Selected Lines into Stock\"\u001b[m action directly from the\u001b[K\r\n  shopping list to create/increment \u001b[1mStock Lots\u001b[m at a chosen \u001b[1mStorage Location\u001b[m (auto-creating and linking catalog\r\n  \u001b[1mComponents\u001b[m for any previously unlinked \u001b[1mBOM Lines\u001b[m).\r\n\u001b[K\u001b[?7l\n\u001b[K  ➡️ \u001b[1mYes — make the Shopping List a live computed view with editable Order Quantity and Supplier/Part # columns,\u001b[?7h\u001b[113G\u001b[m\r\n  \u001b[1msupport both Full CSV export and per-supplier Quick-Order CSV/clipboard formats"]
[0.000, "o", ", and allow receiving lines directly\u001b[m\r\n  \u001b[1minto Stock Lots (or via supplier CSV import).\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[90m────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[34;1m> yes\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[37m○\u001b[m \u001b[37mThought for 15.5s\u001b[m \u001b[37m(Initial hypothesis: missing branches in the design tree could be the root cause. Investigating...)\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[33m●\u001b[m \u001b[33;1mRan\u001b[m \u001b[37m(git status; git log -n 5 --oneline 2>&1 || true)\u001b[m \u001b[37m(ctrl+o to expand)\u001b[?7l\u001b[m\r\n\n\u001b[K\u001b[33;1mCommand\u001b[?7h\u001b[8G\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[90m────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[37;1mRequesting permission for:\u001b[m"]
[0.000, "o", "\r\n\u001b[37m   git status; git log -n 5 --oneline 2>&1 || true\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[1mRun this command?\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[94m> 1. Yes, run command\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n  2. Yes, and always allow in this conversation for commands that start with 'git status'\r\n  3. Yes, and always allow for commands that start with 'git status' (Persist to settings.json)\r\n  4. No, cancel\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\n  \u001b[94;1m↑/↓\u001b[90;22m Navigate · \u001b[94;1mtab\u001b[90;22m Amend · \u001b[94;1mctrl+g\u001b[90;22m edit/expand command\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[?2026l"]
[45.489, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\u001b[0 q\r\u001b[30A  1. \u001b[1mLive Computed View with Inline Overrides\u001b[m: Rather than maintaining a separate stateful \"Purchase Order\" lifecycle,\r\n  the \u001b[1mShopping List\u001b[m is a live computed view over your selected \u001b[1mKit Builds\u001b[m (and optional low-stock restock filter).\r\n  Before exporting, each row lets you edit the \u001b[1mOrder Quantity\u001b[m (initialized to \u001b[1mNet Shortfall\u001b[m, so you can easily bump\r\n  \u001b[94m1x\u001b[m resistor up to \u001b[94m10x\u001b[m or \u001b[94m50x\u001b[m for spares) and select/edit the target \u001b[94mSupplier\u001b[m and \u001b[94mSupplier Part #\u001b[m (pre-filled from\u001b[K\r\n  the linked \u001b[1mComponent\u001b[m's existing \u001b[1mStock Lot\u001b[m supplier metadata).\u001b[K\r\n  2. \u001b[1mExport Formats\u001b[m:\u001b[K\r\n      • \u001b[1mFull Shopping List CSV\u001b[m: Exports all columns (\u001b[94mCategory\u001b[m, \u001b[94mSpec / Component Name\u001b[m, \u001b[94mPackage\u001b[m, \u001b[94mSupplier\u001b[m, \u001b[94mSupplier\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[6C\u001b[94mPart #\u001b[m, \u001b[94mAvailable Stock\u001b[m, \u001b[94mNet Shortfall\u001b[m, \u001b[94mOrder Quantity\u001b[m, \u001b[94mKit Builds & Reference Designators\u001b[m, \u001b[94mNotes\u001b[m), optionally\u001b[?7l\r\n\u001b[K      g"]
[0.000, "o", "rouped or filtered by \u001b[94mSupplier\u001b[m.\u001b[?7h\u001b[39G\r\n      • \u001b[1mSupplier Quick-Order / Cart Format (CSV & Clipboard Copy)\u001b[m: Filters to a selected supplier (e.g., Mouser,\u001b[K\r\n      DigiKey, Tayda, LCSC) and formats \u001b[94mSupplier Part #, Order Quantity, Customer Reference (Kit Build names)\u001b[m for\r\n\u001b[6Cdirect paste or upload into supplier BOM/cart tools.\r\n  3. \u001b[1mClosing the Loop on Arrival\u001b[m: When parts arrive, you can either import the supplier's order CSV via the \u001b[1mComponent\u001b[m\r\n  \u001b[1m& Stock Lot CSV Import\u001b[m workflow (Q1), or use a \u001b[1m\"Receive Selected Lines into Stock\"\u001b[m action directly from the\r\n  shopping list to create/increment \u001b[1mStock Lots\u001b[m at a chosen \u001b[1mStorage Location\u001b[m (auto-creating and linking catalog\r\n  \u001b[1mComponents\u001b[m for any previously unlinked \u001b[1mBOM Lines\u001b[m).\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\u001b[?7l\n\u001b[K  ➡️ \u001b[1mYes — make the Shopping List a live computed view with editable Order Quantity and Supplier/Part # columns,\u001b[?7h\u001b[113G\u001b[m\r\n  \u001b[1msupport both Full CSV export and per-supplier Quick-Ord"]
[0.000, "o", "er CSV/clipboard formats, and allow receiving lines directly\u001b[m\r\n  \u001b[1minto Stock Lots (or via supplier CSV import).\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n\n\u001b[90m────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[34;1m> yes\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n\n\u001b[37m○\u001b[m \u001b[37mThought for 15.5s\u001b[m \u001b[37m(Initial hypothesis: missing branches in the design tree could be the root cause. Investigating...)\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[33m○\u001b[m \u001b[33;1mRunning\u001b[m \u001b[37m(git status; git log -n 5 --oneline 2>&1 || true)\u001b[m \u001b[37m(ctrl+o to expand)\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n⣻  \u001b[94mRunn\u001b[90ming command...\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[90m└ Tip: Use /skills to browse and manage agent skills.\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[90m──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────"]
