[0.100, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\u001b[?25l\u001b[0 q\r\u001b[29A\u001b[33m○\u001b[m \u001b[33;1mEdited\u001b[m 2 files \u001b[37m(GLOSSARY.md, 03-csv-import-and-shopping-list-export-workflows.md)\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[33m○\u001b[m \u001b[33;1mEditing\u001b[m 1 file \u001b[37m(map.md)\u001b[m \u001b[37m(ctrl+o to expand)\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[33;1mPending edit\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[90m────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[37;1m/Users/brett/Demos/audio-inventory-experiment/audio_inventory_skilled/GLOSSARY.md\u001b[m  \u001b[32m+9\u001b[m \u001b[31m-1\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[37m  \u001b[90m 1 \u001b[m    **Bench Log Entry**:\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[37m  \u001b[90m 2 \u001b[m    A timestamped note, voltage/signal measurement, circuit modification, or troubleshooting observation recorded\r\n\t\u001b[37m\u001b[1K against a **Kit Build** during assembly or debugging.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[37m  \u001b[90m 3 \u001b[39;48;2;53;"]
[0.000, "o", "13;14m \u001b[31m-  \u001b[39m_Avoid_: Comment, Audit Log, Ticket Note\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[37m  \u001b[90m 3 \u001b[39;48;2;14;52;15m \u001b[32m+  \u001b[39m_Avoid_: Comment, Audit Log, Ticket Note\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[37m  \u001b[90m 4 \u001b[39;48;2;14;52;15m \u001b[32m+  \u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[37m  \u001b[90m 5 \u001b[39;48;2;14;52;15m \u001b[32m+  \u001b[39m**Shopping List**:\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[37m  \u001b[90m 6 \u001b[39;48;2;14;52;15m \u001b[32m+  \u001b[39mA live computed aggregation of unfulfilled **BOM Line** demand across one or more selected **Kit Builds** (and\u001b[K\u001b[?7l\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[K\u001b[37m     \u001b[48;2;14;52;15m \u001b[32m   \u001b[39moptional low-stock **Components**), grouped by catalog **Component** or normalized specification to calculate  \u001b[?7h\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[4C\u001b[37m\u001b[1K \u001b[48;2;14;52;15m \u001b[32m   \u001b[39m**Net Shortfall** and export supplier order files.\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[37m  \u001b[90m 7 \u001b[39;48;2;14;52;15m \u001b[32m+  \u001b[39m_Avoid_: Purchase Order, Requisition, Cart\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[37m  \u001b[90m 8 \u001b[39;48;2;14;52;15m \u001b[32m+  \u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[37m  \u001b[90m 9 \u001b[39;48;2;14;52;15m \u001b[32m+  \u001b[39m**Net Shortfall**:\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[37m  \u001b[90m10 \u001b[39;48;2;14;52;15m \u001b[32m+  \u001b[39mThe additional qu"]
[0.000, "o", "antity of a **Component** (or unlinked specification) that must be purchased across a selected\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[4C\u001b[37m\u001b[1K \u001b[48;2;14;52;15m \u001b[32m   \u001b[39mset of **Kit Builds**, equal to the total unallocated quantity required across those builds minus current\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[4C\u001b[37m\u001b[1K \u001b[48;2;14;52;15m \u001b[32m   \u001b[39m**Available Stock** (floored at zero).\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[37m  \u001b[90m11 \u001b[39;48;2;14;52;15m \u001b[32m+  \u001b[39m_Avoid_: Deficit, Backorder Quantity, Negative Balance\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[K\n  \u001b[94;1mshift+tab\u001b[90;22m to auto-approve file edits\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[1mAccept this file edit?\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[94m> 1. Yes, accept this change\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n  2. No, reject this change\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\n  \u001b[94;1m↑/↓\u001b[90;22m Navigate · \u001b[94;1mtab\u001b[90;22m Amend · \u001b[94;1mf\u001b[90;22m full diff\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[?2026l"]
[20.792, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\u001b[0 q\r\n\u001b[J\u001b[31A  Before exporting, each row lets you edit the \u001b[1mOrder Quantity\u001b[m (initialized to \u001b[1mNet Shortfall\u001b[m, so you can easily bump\r\n  \u001b[94m1x\u001b[m resistor up to \u001b[94m10x\u001b[m or \u001b[94m50x\u001b[m for spares) and select/edit the target \u001b[94mSupplier\u001b[m and \u001b[94mSupplier Part #\u001b[m (pre-filled from\r\n  the linked \u001b[1mComponent\u001b[m's existing \u001b[1mStock Lot\u001b[m supplier metadata).\r\n  2. \u001b[1mExport Formats\u001b[m:\n\u001b[15D\u001b[1K • \u001b[1mFull Shopping List CSV\u001b[m: Exports all columns (\u001b[94mCategory\u001b[m, \u001b[94mSpec / Component Name\u001b[m, \u001b[94mPackage\u001b[m, \u001b[94mSupplier\u001b[m, \u001b[94mSupplier\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[6C\u001b[94mPart #\u001b[m, \u001b[94mAvailable Stock\u001b[m, \u001b[94mNet Shortfall\u001b[m, \u001b[94mOrder Quantity\u001b[m, \u001b[94mKit Builds & Reference Designators\u001b[m, \u001b[94mNotes\u001b[m), optionally\r\n\u001b[5C\u001b[1K grouped or filtered by \u001b[94mSupplier\u001b[m.\u001b[K\n\u001b[33D\u001b[1K • \u001b[1mSupplier Quick-Order / Cart Format (CSV & Clipboard Copy)\u001b[m: Filters to a selected supplier (e.g., Mouser,\r\n\u001b[5C\u001b[1K DigiKey, Tayda, LCSC) and formats \u001b[94mSupplier Part #, Order Quantity, Customer R"]
[0.000, "o", "eference (Kit Build names)\u001b[m for\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[5C\u001b[1K direct paste or upload into supplier BOM/cart tools.\u001b[K\r\n  3. \u001b[1mClosing the Loop on Arrival\u001b[m: When parts arrive, you can either import the supplier's order CSV via the \u001b[1mComponent\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n  \u001b[1m& Stock Lot CSV Import\u001b[m workflow (Q1), or use a \u001b[1m\"Receive Selected Lines into Stock\"\u001b[m action directly from the\u001b[K\r\n  shopping list to create/increment \u001b[1mStock Lots\u001b[m at a chosen \u001b[1mStorage Location\u001b[m (auto-creating and linking catalog\u001b[K\r\n  \u001b[1mComponents\u001b[m for any previously unlinked \u001b[1mBOM Lines\u001b[m).\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\u001b[?7l\n\u001b[K  ➡️ \u001b[1mYes — make the Shopping List a live computed view with editable Order Quantity and Supplier/Part # columns,\u001b[?7h\u001b[113G\u001b[m\r\n  \u001b[1msupport both Full CSV export and per-supplier Quick-Order CSV/clipboard formats, and allow receiving lines directly\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n  \u001b[1minto Stock Lots (or via supplier CSV import).\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[90m────────────────────────────────────"]
