[0.017, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\u001b[29A1. \"Choose the ticket. If the user named one, use it. Otherwise take the first frontier ticket in order. \u001b[1mClaim it\u001b[m:\r\n  assign it to yourself before any work.\"\u001b[K\r\n  In \u001b[94missue-tracker-local.md\u001b[m:\u001b[K\r\n  \"- \u001b[1mClaim\u001b[m: set \u001b[94mStatus: claimed\u001b[m and save before any work.\"\r\n  2. \"Resolve it as the type its \u001b[94mwayfinder:<type>\u001b[m label names (see \u001b[1mTicket Types\u001b[m). Read the label, not just the body:\r\n  the body never states the type. \u001b[1mZoom as needed\u001b[m: fetch the full body of any related or closed ticket on demand; call\r\n\u001b[6CSkill tool for whichever skills the \u001b[94m## Notes\u001b[m block names. If in doubt, call the Skill tool twice, for\u001b[K\r\n  \"grilling\" and \"domain-modeling\".\"\u001b[K\r\n  Also in \u001b[94mmap.md\u001b[m:\u001b[K\r\n  \"- \u001b[1mSkills\u001b[m: Every session resolving a ticket should consult \u001b[94mgrilling\u001b[m and \u001b[94mdomain-modeling\u001b[m (and \u001b[94mprototype\u001b[m for\r\n  prototype tickets, \u001b[94mcodebase-design\u001b[m when designing module boundaries).\"\u001b[K\r\n  Since ticket 04 is about crate and app architectur"]
[0.000, "o", "e and how domain modules should be structured, let's also read\r\n  \u001b[94mcodebase-design/SKILL.md\u001b[m! And let's claim \u001b[94m04-rust-htmx-turso-crate-and-app-architecture.md\u001b[m right now. Let's do both\r\n  in parallel.\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[32m●\u001b[m \u001b[33;1mEdited\u001b[m 1 file \u001b[37m(04-rust-htmx-turso-crate-and-app-architecture.md)\u001b[m\n\u001b[63D\u001b[33;1mxplored\u001b[m 1 file \u001b[37m(SKILL.md)\u001b[m \u001b[37m(ctrl+o to expand)\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[37m▸ Thought for 13s\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[K\n  I have loaded the \u001b[34;4m\u001b]8;id=jkc1646cb95cca4622;file:///Users/brett/Demos/audio-inventory-experiment/audio_inventory_skilled/.scratch/audio-inventory/map.md\u0007Wayfinder Map\u001b[m\u001b]8;;\u0007 and claimed the next unblocked frontier ticket:\r\n  \u001b[34;4m\u001b]8;id=jkd5f35ec8c5206785;file:///Users/brett/Demos/audio-inventory-experiment/audio_inventory_skilled/.scratch/audio-inventory/issues/04-rust-htmx-turso-crate-and-app-architecture.md\u0007Rust + HTMX + Local Turso Crate & App Architecture\u001b[m\u001b]8;;\u0007.\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\n  Let's work through the architectural decisions one question at a time.\r\n  ──────"]
