[0.000, "o", "quantity adjustments, \u001b[1mBOM Line\u001b[m status toggles, and CSV reconciliation rows), we\u001b[?7h\u001b[114G\r\n  need to pick our HTTP router, HTML templating approach, and CSS strategy:\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\n  1. \u001b[1mHTTP + HTML Macros (\u001b[94;22maxum\u001b[39;1m + \u001b[94;22mmaud\u001b[39;1m + zero-Node static CSS)\u001b[m:\r\n      • \u001b[94maxum\u001b[m (\u001b[94mtokio\u001b[m + \u001b[94mtower-http\u001b[m) for routing, multipart uploads, and static assets.\r\n\t\u001b[94mmaud\u001b[m for compile-time HTML macros in pure Rust—every page layout and HTMX partial (e.g., a single \u001b[94mBOM Line\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[6C\u001b[94m<tr>\u001b[m or \u001b[94mAvailable Stock\u001b[m badge) is just a Rust function returning \u001b[94mMarkup\u001b[m, making it effortless to return either\r\n\u001b[6Ca full page or a targeted HTMX fragment from the same handler without keeping separate \u001b[94m.html\u001b[m files in sync.\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[6C• A self-contained static CSS stylesheet (dense tabular workbench layout with CSS variables) and vendored \u001b[94mhtmx.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[6C\u001b[94mmin.js\u001b[m embedded/served directly by the Rust binary, requiring \u001b[1mzero Node.js/npm build toolchain\u001b"]
[0.000, "o", "[m.\u001b[K\r\n  2. \u001b[1mHTTP + Jinja-style Templates (\u001b[94;22maxum\u001b[39;1m + \u001b[94;22maskama\u001b[39;1m or \u001b[94;22mminijinja\u001b[39;1m)\u001b[m:\u001b[K\r\n      • Separate \u001b[94m.html\u001b[m template files using Jinja syntax, compiled into Rust structs (\u001b[94maskama\u001b[m) or loaded at runtime\r\n\u001b[6C(\u001b[94mminijinja\u001b[m).\u001b[K\r\n  3. \u001b[1mOther preference\u001b[m (e.g., \u001b[94mactix-web\u001b[m, Tailwind CLI build step, etc.).\r\n\u001b[K\u001b[?7l\n\u001b[K  ➡️ \u001b[1mUse\u001b[?7h\u001b[9G\u001b[m\r\n⣷  \u001b[94mWo\u001b[90mrking...\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[90m────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[94m>\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[90m────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────"]
