[0.034, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\u001b[29A1. \u001b[1mOfficial \u001b[94;22mlibsql\u001b[39;1m Crate + Embedded Startup SQL Migrations + Parameterized SQL\u001b[m:\r\n      • \u001b[1mDriver\u001b[m: Official \u001b[94mlibsql\u001b[m crate initialized via \u001b[94mlibsql::Builder::new_local(&db_path)\u001b[m (which supports local file\r\n\u001b[6Cpersistence out of the box and can optionally sync to remote Turso later if ever desired), configured on\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[6Cstartup with \u001b[94mPRAGMA foreign_keys = ON\u001b[m and \u001b[94mPRAGMA journal_mode = WAL\u001b[m.\u001b[K\n\u001b[68D• \u001b[1mMigrations\u001b[m: Numbered \u001b[94m.sql\u001b[m files in \u001b[94mmigrations/\u001b[m embedded into the binary via \u001b[94minclude_str!\u001b[m and applied\r\n\u001b[6Cautomatically on startup in a transaction (tracked in a \u001b[94m_schema_migrations\u001b[m table).\u001b[K\n\u001b[82D• \u001b[1mQueries\u001b[m: Parameterized SQL inside our repository implementation (with a small dynamic \u001b[94mWHERE\u001b[m-clause builder\r\n\u001b[6Cfor parametric \u001b[94mspecs_json\u001b[m filters and multi-build \u001b[1mShopping List\u001b[m aggregation), avoiding heavy ORM macro overhead\r\n\u001b[6Cthat struggles with SQLite recursive CTEs and \u001b[94m"]
[0.000, "o", "json_extract\u001b[m.\u001b[K\r\n  2. \u001b[94msqlx\u001b[39;1m (SQLite driver) or an ORM (\u001b[94;22msea-orm\u001b[39;1m / \u001b[94;22mdiesel\u001b[39;1m)\u001b[m:\u001b[K\r\n      • Uses standard SQLite driver rather than native \u001b[94mlibsql\u001b[m, or adds ORM entity layers.\r\n\u001b[K\u001b[?7l\n\n\u001b[K  ➡️ \u001b[1mUse Option 1 (the official \u001b[94;22mlibsql\u001b[39;1m crate in local-file mode with \u001b[94;22mWAL\u001b[39;1m + \u001b[94;22mforeign_keys = ON\u001b[39;1m, embedded\u001b[?7h\u001b[103G\u001b[?7l\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[K  \u001b[94mmigrations/*.sql\u001b[39;1m auto-applied on startup, and direct parameterized SQL with a lightweight filter builder for\u001b[?7h\u001b[111G\u001b[m\r\n  \u001b[94mjson_extract\u001b[39;1m and recursive CTEs)\u001b[m — sound good?\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[90m────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[34;1m> https://crates.io/crates/turso\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[37m○\u001b[m \u001b[37mThought for 41.8s\u001b[m \u001b[37m(Initial investigation suggests an ADR update is needed to reflect the `turso` crate dependency...)\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[32m"]
