[0.017, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\r\u001b[29A  ➡️ \u001b[1mUse Option 1 (the official \u001b[m\u001b[94mlibsql\u001b[m\u001b[1m crate in local-file mode with \u001b[m\u001b[94mWAL\u001b[m\u001b[1m + \u001b[m\u001b[94mforeign_keys = ON\u001b[m\u001b[1m, embedded\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[?5W\u001b[J  \u001b[94mmigrations/*.sql\u001b[39;1m auto-applied on startup, and direct parameterized SQL with a lightweight filter builder for\u001b[m\r\n  \u001b[94mjson_extract\u001b[39;1m and recursive CTEs)\u001b[m — sound good?\r\n\n\u001b[90m────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[34;1m> https://crates.io/crates/turso\u001b[m\r\n\n\u001b[37m○\u001b[m \u001b[37mThought for 41.8s\u001b[m \u001b[37m(Initial investigation suggests an ADR update is needed to reflect the `turso` crate dependency...)\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[32m●\u001b[m \u001b[33;1mExplored\u001b[m 2 searches \u001b[37m(+1 · \"turso\" crate rust sqlite compatibility json_extract OR recursive CTE OR foreign keys)\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[32m●\u001b[m \u001b[33;1mEdited\u001b[m 1 file \u001b[37m(0001-rust-htmx-turso-stack.md)\u001b[m \u001b[37m(ctrl+o to expand)\u001b[m\r\n\n  Got it—w"]
[0.000, "o", "e'll use the native Rust \u001b[94mturso\u001b[m crate (\u001b[94mturso::Builder::new_local\u001b[m), with embedded \u001b[94mmigrations/*.sql\u001b[m applied on\r\n  startup and parameterized SQL queries. I also updated \u001b[34;4m\u001b]8;id=jk2093e247ad751bcf;file:///Users/brett/Demos/audio-inventory-experiment/audio_inventory_skilled/docs/adr/0001-rust-htmx-turso-stack.md\u00070001-rust-htmx-turso-stack.md\u001b[m\u001b]8;;\u0007 to reflect the \u001b[94mturso\u001b[m crate\r\n  specifically.\r\n  ──────\u001b[?7l\r\n\u001b[K  ❓ \u001b[1mQ3\u001b[m - \u001b[1mLocal Data Directory Layout, Attachments & Backup/Restore\u001b[m: \u001b[1mKit Builds\u001b[m and \u001b[1mBench Log Entries\u001b[m support\u001b[?7h\u001b[110G\r\n  uploaded schematic PDFs, build docs, and bench photos, and the map notes we need a clean story for backing up the\r\n  local Turso database alongside those attachments:\r\n\n  1. \u001b[1mSingle Self-Contained Data Directory + 1-Click ZIP Backup/Restore\u001b[m:\n\u001b[65D• \u001b[1mData Directory (\u001b[94;22mDATA_DIR\u001b[39;1m, defaulting to \u001b[94;22m./data\u001b[39;1m or configurable via \u001b[94;22m--data-dir\u001b[39;1m / \u001b[94;22mAUDIO_INVENTORY_D"]
[0.000, "o", "ATA_DIR\u001b[39;1m)\u001b[m:\r\n\t  • \u001b[94mdata/inventory.db\u001b[m (plus \u001b[94m.db-wal\u001b[m / \u001b[94m.db-shm\u001b[m) for the local \u001b[94mturso\u001b[m database.\r\n\t  • \u001b[94mdata/attachments/<kit_build_id>/<uuid>-<sanitized_filename>\u001b[m on disk, with metadata (\u001b[94mid\u001b[m, \u001b[94mkit_build_id\u001b[m,\r\n\t  \u001b[94mbench_log_entry_id\u001b[m, \u001b[94moriginal_filename\u001b[m, \u001b[94mmime_type\u001b[m, \u001b[94mrelative_path\u001b[m, \u001b[94msize_bytes\u001b[m, \u001b[94mcreated_at\u001b[m) tracked in an\r\n\t  \u001b[94mattachment\u001b[m\r\n\n\n⣟  \u001b[90mGenerating...\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[90m└ Tip: To disable tips, toggle Show Tips in /settings.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[90m────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[94m>\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[90m────────────────────────────────"]
