[0.019, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\r\u001b[29A\u001b[90m────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[34;1m> https://crates.io/crates/turso\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[37m○\u001b[m \u001b[37mThought for 41.8s\u001b[m \u001b[37m(Initial investigation suggests an ADR update is needed to reflect the `turso` crate dependency...)\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[32m●\u001b[m \u001b[33;1mExplored\u001b[m 2 searches \u001b[37m(+1 · \"turso\" crate rust sqlite compatibility json_extract OR recursive CTE OR foreign keys)\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[3C\u001b[33;1mdited\u001b[m 1 file \u001b[37m(0001-rust-htmx-turso-stack.md)\u001b[m \u001b[37m(ctrl+o to expand)\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\n  Got it—we'll use the native Rust \u001b[94mturso\u001b[m crate (\u001b[94mturso::Builder::new_local\u001b[m), with embedded \u001b[94mmigrations/*.sql\u001b[m applied on\r\n  startup and parameterized SQL queries. I also updated \u001b[34;4m\u001b]8;id=jkc70a23e79da1b093;file:///Users/brett/Demos/audio-inventory-experiment/audio_inventory_skilled/docs/adr/0001-rust-htmx-turso-stack.md\u00070001-rust-htmx-turso-s"]
[0.000, "o", "tack.md\u001b[m\u001b]8;;\u0007 to reflect the \u001b[94mturso\u001b[m crate\u001b[K\r\n  specifically.\u001b[K\r\n  ──────\u001b[K\u001b[?7l\r\n\u001b[K  ❓ \u001b[1mQ3\u001b[m - \u001b[1mLocal Data Directory Layout, Attachments & Backup/Restore\u001b[m: \u001b[1mKit Builds\u001b[m and \u001b[1mBench Log Entries\u001b[m support\u001b[?7h\u001b[110G\u001b[?7l\r\n\u001b[K  uploaded schematic PDFs, build docs, and bench photos, and the map notes we need a clean story for backing up the\u001b[?7h\u001b[116G\r\n  local Turso database alongside those attachments:\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\n  1. \u001b[1mSingle Self-Contained Data Directory + 1-Click ZIP Backup/Restore\u001b[m:\r\n      • \u001b[1mData Directory (\u001b[94;22mDATA_DIR\u001b[39;1m, defaulting to \u001b[94;22m./data\u001b[39;1m or configurable via \u001b[94;22m--data-dir\u001b[39;1m / \u001b[94;22mAUDIO_INVENTORY_DATA_DIR\u001b[39;1m)\u001b[m:\r\n\u001b[6C    • \u001b[94mdata/inventory.db\u001b[m (plus \u001b[94m.db-wal\u001b[m / \u001b[94m.db-shm\u001b[m) for the local \u001b[94mturso\u001b[m database.\u001b[K\n\u001b[67D\u001b[94mattachments/<kit_build_id>/<uuid>-<sanitized_filename>\u001b[m on disk, with metadata (\u001b[94mid\u001b[m, \u001b[94mkit_build_id\u001b[m,\r\n\t  \u001b[94mbench_log_entry_id\u001b[m, \u001b[94moriginal_filename\u001b[m"]
[0.000, "o", ", \u001b[94mmime_type\u001b[m, \u001b[94mrelative_path\u001b[m, \u001b[94msize_bytes\u001b[m, \u001b[94mcreated_at\u001b[m) tracked in an\u001b[K\r\n\t  \u001b[94mattachments\u001b[m table.\u001b[K\n\u001b[22D• \u001b[1mBackup & Restore\u001b[m:\u001b[K\n\u001b[19D    • An in-app \u001b[1mExport Backup (\u001b[94;22m.zip\u001b[39;1m)\u001b[m endpoint (\u001b[94mGET /settings/backup.zip\u001b[m) that checkpoints/reads a consistent\r\n\t  snapshot of \u001b[94mi\u001b[m\u001b[K\n\n\n\u001b[20D\u001b[90mG\u001b[94menera\u001b[m\n\n\n\u001b[7D\u001b[?2026l"]
