[0.018, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\r\u001b[28A  startup and parameterized SQL queries. I also updated \u001b]8;id=jkd64e45a0bba48405;file:///Users/brett/Demos/audio-inventory-experiment/audio_inventory_skilled/docs/adr/0001-rust-htmx-turso-stack.md\u001b\\\u001b[4;34;4m0\u001b[m\u001b[4;34;4m0\u001b[m\u001b[4;34;4m0\u001b[m\u001b[4;34;4m1\u001b[m\u001b[4;34;4m-\u001b[m\u001b[4;34;4mr\u001b[m\u001b[4;34;4mu\u001b[m\u001b[4;34;4ms\u001b[m\u001b[4;34;4mt\u001b[m\u001b[4;34;4m-\u001b[m\u001b[4;34;4mh\u001b[m\u001b[4;34;4mt\u001b[m\u001b[4;34;4mm\u001b[m\u001b[4;34;4mx\u001b[m\u001b[4;34;4m-\u001b[m\u001b[4;34;4mt\u001b[m\u001b[4;34;4mu\u001b[m\u001b[4;34;4mr\u001b[m\u001b[4;34;4ms\u001b[m\u001b[4;34;4mo\u001b[m\u001b[4;34;4m-\u001b[m\u001b[4;34;4ms\u001b[m\u001b[4;34;4mt\u001b[m\u001b[4;34;4ma\u001b[m\u001b[4;34;4mc\u001b[m\u001b[4;34;4mk\u001b[m\u001b[4;34;4m.\u001b[m\u001b[4;34;4mm\u001b[m\u001b[4;34;4md\u001b[m\u001b]8;;\u001b\\ to reflect the \u001b[94mturso\u001b[m crate\u001b[K\r\n  specifically.\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[?5W\u001b[J  ──────\u001b[?7l\r\n\u001b[K  ❓ \u001b[1mQ3\u001b[m - \u001b[1mLocal Data Directory Layout, Attachments & Backup/Restore\u001b[m: \u001b[1mKit Builds\u001b[m and \u001b[1mBench Log Entries\u001b[m support\u001b[?7h\u001b[110G\r\n  uploaded schematic PDFs, build docs, and bench photos, and the map notes we need a clean story for backing up the\r\n  local Turso database alongside those attachments:\r\n\n  1. \u001b["]
[0.000, "o", "1mSingle Self-Contained Data Directory + 1-Click ZIP Backup/Restore\u001b[m:\n\u001b[65D• \u001b[1mData Directory (\u001b[94;22mDATA_DIR\u001b[39;1m, defaulting to \u001b[94;22m./data\u001b[39;1m or configurable via \u001b[94;22m--data-dir\u001b[39;1m / \u001b[94;22mAUDIO_INVENTORY_DATA_DIR\u001b[39;1m)\u001b[m:\r\n\t  • \u001b[94mdata/inventory.db\u001b[m (plus \u001b[94m.db-wal\u001b[m / \u001b[94m.db-shm\u001b[m) for the local \u001b[94mturso\u001b[m database.\r\n\t  • \u001b[94mdata/attachments/<kit_build_id>/<uuid>-<sanitized_filename>\u001b[m on disk, with metadata (\u001b[94mid\u001b[m, \u001b[94mkit_build_id\u001b[m,\r\n\t  \u001b[94mbench_log_entry_id\u001b[m, \u001b[94moriginal_filename\u001b[m, \u001b[94mmime_type\u001b[m, \u001b[94mrelative_path\u001b[m, \u001b[94msize_bytes\u001b[m, \u001b[94mcreated_at\u001b[m) tracked in an\r\n\t  \u001b[94mattachments\u001b[m table.\n\u001b[22D• \u001b[1mBackup & Restore\u001b[m:\r\n\t  • An in-app \u001b[1mExport Backup (\u001b[94;22m.zip\u001b[39;1m)\u001b[m endpoint (\u001b[94mGET /settings/backup.zip\u001b[m) that checkpoints/reads a consistent\r\n\t  snapshot of \u001b[94minventory.db\u001b[m and bundles it with \u001b[94mdata/attachments/\u001b[m into a single \u001b[94m.zip\u001b[m archive download.\r\n\t  • A \u001b[1mRestore / CLI backu"]
[0.000, "o", "p\u001b[m workflow so moving machines or snapshotting before a big import is just copying or\r\n\t  unzipping one folder.\r\n\n  2. \u001b[1mStore Attachments as SQL BLOBs inside \u001b[94;22minventory.db\u001b[m:\n\u001b[50D• Keeps everything in a single \u001b[94m.db\u001b[m file, though large PDF schematics and high-res bench photos bloat the\r\n\u001b[6Cdatabase file.\u001b[?7l\r\n\n\n\u001b[K  ➡️ \u001b[1mUse Option 1 (a unified \u001b[94;22mdata/\u001b[39;1m directory holding \u001b[94;22minventory.db\u001b[39;1m and \u001b[94;22mdata/attachments/<kit_build_id>/...\u001b[39;1m, plus an \u001b[?7h\u001b[116G\u001b[m\r\n  \u001b[1min-app 1-click \u001b[94;22m.zip\u001b[39;1m backup download bundling the database and attachments)\u001b[m — does that work for you?\r\n\n\u001b[90m────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[34;1m> sgtm\u001b[m\r\n⡿  \u001b[90mGe\u001b[94mnerat\u001b[90ming...\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[90m────────────────────────────────────────"]
