[0.016, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\u001b[29A2. \u001b[1mStore Attachments as SQL BLOBs inside \u001b[94;22minventory.db\u001b[m:\r\n      • Keeps everything in a single \u001b[94m.db\u001b[m file, though large PDF schematics and high-res bench photos bloat the\r\n\u001b[6Cdatabase file.\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\u001b[?7l\n\n\u001b[K  ➡️ \u001b[1mUse Option 1 (a unified \u001b[94;22mdata/\u001b[39;1m directory holding \u001b[94;22minventory.db\u001b[39;1m and \u001b[94;22mdata/attachments/<kit_build_id>/...\u001b[39;1m, plus an \u001b[?7h\u001b[116G\u001b[?7l\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[K  \u001b[1min-app 1-click \u001b[94;22m.zip\u001b[39;1m backup download bundling the database and attachments)\u001b[m — does that work for you?\u001b[?7h\u001b[103G\r\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[90m────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[34;1m> sgtm\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[37m▸ Thought for 24s\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[K\u001b[?7l\n\u001b[K  ❓ \u001b[1mQ4\u001b[m - \u001b[1mCrate Layout, Deep Module Boundaries & Test Seam\u001b[m: Following the \u001b[34;4m\u001b]8;id=jk88bb2cff69057b73;file:///Users/brett/Demos/audio-inventory-experiment/audio_inventory_"]
[0.000, "o", "skilled/.agents/skills/codebase-design/SKILL.md\u0007codebase-design\u001b[m\u001b]8;;\u0007 principles, we want \u001b[1mdeep\u001b[?7h\u001b[115G\u001b[?7l\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[K  \u001b[1mmodules\u001b[m with small interfaces and rich domain implementations—avoiding shallow pass-through service/repository\u001b[?7h\u001b[113G\r\n  ceremony—and a single real test seam:\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\n  1. \u001b[1mSingle Cargo Package with 5 Deep Domain Modules + Thin Web/HTML Adapter\u001b[m:\r\n      • \u001b[94mspec_parser\u001b[39;1m (Pure Rust module)\u001b[m: Small interface (\u001b[94mparse_spec(raw_text, category_hint) -> ParsedSpec\u001b[m and\r\n\u001b[6C\u001b[94minfer_category_from_designators(designators) -> Option<Category>\u001b[m) hiding all unit normalization (\u001b[94m4k7\u001b[m → \u001b[94m4700.0 Ω\u001b[m,\r\n\u001b[6C\u001b[94m100nF\u001b[m → \u001b[94m1e-7 F\u001b[m), tolerance/wattage/voltage/package extraction, and reference-designator rules. Used across\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[6Cmanual entry, BOM creation, CSV import, and Shopping List matching.\u001b[K\n\u001b[67D• \u001b[94mcatalog\u001b[39;1m (Turso-backed module)\u001b[m: Owns \u001b[1mComponents\u001b[m, the recursive \u001b[1mStorage Location\u001b[m hierarchy, and \u001b[1mSto"]
[0.000, "o", "ck\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[6C\u001b[1mLots\u001b[m—hiding dynamic \u001b[94mspecs_json\u001b[m SQL filtering, recursive CTE path resolution (\u001b[94mCrate A > Op-Amps Bag\u001b[m), \u001b[94mAvailable\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[6C\u001b[94mStock\u001b[m computation, and automatic lot merging when moving/adding stock t\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\n⣯  \u001b[94mG\u001b[90menerating...\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[90m└ Tip: Use /diff to view uncommitted changes in your workspace.\u001b[m\n\n\u001b[61D\u001b[?2026l"]
