[0.017, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\r\u001b[29A      • \u001b[1mVariant C (\u001b[m\u001b[94m?variant=C\u001b[m\u001b[1m — Split-Screen Kitting Console + Bench HUD)\u001b[m: Side-by-side \u001b[1mKit Build BOM\u001b[m (left 60%) and\u001b[K\r\n      live \u001b[1mComponent Catalog Search\u001b[m (right 40%) so clicking a BOM line's 🔍 button filters the catalog on the right\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[?5W\u001b[J\u001b[6Cfor 1-click kitting/substitution, plus a dedicated \u001b[1mSoldering Bench HUD\u001b[m toggle.\n\u001b[78D• \u001b[1mLive HTMX-style state interactions\u001b[m: Type shorthand like \u001b[94m4k7\u001b[m or \u001b[94m0.047uF\u001b[m into the search bar, click \u001b[94m+\u001b[m / \u001b[94m−\u001b[m on\r\n\u001b[6C\u001b[1mStock Lots\u001b[m, merge duplicate lots, click \u001b[94mUnallocated\u001b[m / \u001b[94mReserved\u001b[m / \u001b[94mPicked\u001b[m / \u001b[94mInstalled\u001b[m status transitions on \u001b[1mBOM\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[6C\u001b[1mLines\u001b[m, split the \u001b[94mD1, D2\u001b[m germanium diode line, substitute \u001b[94mBAT41\u001b[m, or tap individual reference designators (\u001b[94m[R1]\u001b[m,\r\n\u001b[6C\u001b[94m[C3]\u001b[m) in the bench checklist.\r\n\n  ──────\u001b[?7l\r\n\u001b[K  ❓ \u001b[1mQ1\u001b[m — \u001b[1mOverall Workbench Layout & Navigation Structure\u001b[m: After flippin"]
[0.000, "o", "g through Variants A, B, and C in\u001b[?7h\u001b[106G\r\n  \u001b[34;4m\u001b]8;id=jk7d145c14734dd784;file:///Users/brett/Demos/audio-inventory-experiment/audio_inventory_skilled/.scratch/audio-inventory/prototype-ui.html\u0007prototype-ui.html\u001b[m\u001b]8;;\u0007, which primary layout paradigm (or hybrid of features from A, B, and C) feels right for the app?\r\n\n  1. \u001b[1mVariant A (Full-Width Dense Workbench Table + Slide-Over Inspector Drawer)\u001b[m as the primary layout across\r\n  \u001b[1mComponent Catalog\u001b[m and \u001b[1mKit Build BOM\u001b[m, with \u001b[1mVariant C's Split-Screen Catalog Drawer / Candidate Finder\u001b[m opening on\r\n  demand when linking, substituting, or kitting a \u001b[1mBOM Line\u001b[m, and \u001b[1mVariant C's interactive Reference Designator chips\u001b[m\r\n  \u001b[1m(\u001b[94;22m[R1]\u001b[39;1m, \u001b[94;22m[R2]\u001b[39;1m) + Bench Log split\u001b[m for the active \u001b[1mBench Checklist\u001b[m view.\r\n  2. \u001b[1mVariant B (Three-Pane Master-Detail IDE Layout)\u001b[m everywhere, keeping the \u001b[1mStorage Location\u001b[m / \u001b[1mKit Build\u001b[m tree\r\n  permanently pinned on the left and the inspector permanently pin"]
[0.000, "o", "ned on the right.\r\n  3. \u001b[1mVariant C (Split-Screen Kitting Console)\u001b[m as the default \u001b[1mKit Build\u001b[m layout at all times.\u001b[?7l\r\n\n\u001b[K  ➡️ \u001b[1mRecommendation: Option 1 (Variant A's full-width dense tables + slide-over inspector drawer as the core shell,\u001b[?7h\u001b[116G\u001b[m\r\n  \u001b[1mborrowing Variant B's collapsible Storage Location filter tree for the Catalog view and Variant C's interactive \u001b[m\r\n  \u001b[1mper-designator \u001b[94;22m[R1]\u001b[39;1m \u001b[94;22m[R2]\u001b[39;1m chips + side-by-side Bench Log for the Active Bench view).\u001b[m Full-width tables give maximum\r\n  breathing room for parametric columns, verbatim specs, and inline HTMX steppers, while sliding open the right-hand\r\n  inspector/catalog drawer on demand gives you Variant C's side-by-side kitting power without permanently cramping\r\n  the table columns. Does that combination match what you want?\r\n  ──────\r\n  \u001b[1m### Mo\u001b[m\r\n⢿  \u001b[90mGener\u001b[94mating\u001b[90m...\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[90m└ Tip: Use @ to mention files and give the model more context.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[90m─────"]
