[0.033, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\u001b[29A──────\u001b[?7l\r\n\u001b[K  ❓ \u001b[1mQ1\u001b[m — \u001b[1mOverall Workbench Layout & Navigation Structure\u001b[m: After flipping through Variants A, B, and C in\u001b[?7h\u001b[106G\u001b[?7l\r\n\u001b[K  \u001b[34;4m\u001b]8;id=jkc0a9229fe8560540;file:///Users/brett/Demos/audio-inventory-experiment/audio_inventory_skilled/.scratch/audio-inventory/prototype-ui.html\u0007prototype-ui.html\u001b[m\u001b]8;;\u0007, which primary layout paradigm (or hybrid of features from A, B, and C) feels right for the app?\u001b[?7h\u001b[117G\r\n\u001b[K\n  1. \u001b[1mVariant A (Full-Width Dense Workbench Table + Slide-Over Inspector Drawer)\u001b[m as the primary layout across\r\n  \u001b[1mComponent Catalog\u001b[m and \u001b[1mKit Build BOM\u001b[m, with \u001b[1mVariant C's Split-Screen Catalog Drawer / Candidate Finder\u001b[m opening on\r\n  demand when linking, substituting, or kitting a \u001b[1mBOM Line\u001b[m, and \u001b[1mVariant C's interactive Reference Designator chips\u001b[m\r\n  \u001b[1m(\u001b[94;22m[R1]\u001b[39;1m, \u001b[94;22m[R2]\u001b[39;1m) + Bench Log split\u001b[m for the active \u001b[1mBench Checklist\u001b[m view.\u001b[K\r\n  2. \u001b[1mVariant B (Three-Pane Master-Detail"]
[0.000, "o", " IDE Layout)\u001b[m everywhere, keeping the \u001b[1mStorage Location\u001b[m / \u001b[1mKit Build\u001b[m tree\r\n  permanently pinned on the left and the inspector permanently pinned on the right.\u001b[K\r\n  3. \u001b[1mVariant C (Split-Screen Kitting Console)\u001b[m as the default \u001b[1mKit Build\u001b[m layout at all times.\r\n\u001b[K\u001b[?7l\n\u001b[K  ➡️ \u001b[1mRecommendation: Option 1 (Variant A's full-width dense tables + slide-over inspector drawer as the core shell,\u001b[?7h\u001b[116G\u001b[?7l\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[K  \u001b[1mborrowing Variant B's collapsible Storage Location filter tree for the Catalog view and Variant C's interactive \u001b[?7h\u001b[115G\u001b[m\r\n  \u001b[1mper-designator \u001b[94;22m[R1]\u001b[39;1m \u001b[94;22m[R2]\u001b[39;1m chips + side-by-side Bench Log for the Active Bench view).\u001b[m Full-width tables give maximum\r\n  breathing room for parametric columns, verbatim specs, and inline HTMX steppers, while sliding open the right-hand\r\n  inspector/catalog drawer on demand gives you Variant C's side-by-side kitting power without permanently cramping\u001b[K\r\n  the table columns. Does that combination match what y"]
[0.000, "o", "ou want?\u001b[K\r\n  ──────\u001b[K\r\n  \u001b[1m### Modern Web Guidance\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[K\n  • \u001b[94mresponsive-table\u001b[m: Wrapped data tables in focusable \u001b[94mrole=\"region\"\u001b[m containers with \u001b[94mcontainer-type: inline-size\u001b[m,\r\n  sticky column (\u001b[94mthead\u001b[m) and row (\u001b[94mtbody th\u001b[m) headers, and a \u001b[94m@container (width < 600px)\u001b[m stacked card transformation\u001b[K\r\n  using CSS custom properties for cell labels (\"Use \u001b[94m@container\u001b[m queries instead of \u001b[94m@media\u001b[m queries.\" / \u001b[94m\"/* MANDATORY:\u001b[m\r\n  \u001b[94mHide column header from layout and screen readers. */\"\u001b[m).\u001b[K\r\n  •\u001b[K\n\n\n\n\b\u001b[?2026l"]
