[0.399, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\r\u001b[28A\u001b[K\r\n  ➡️ \u001b[1mRecommendation: Option 1 (Variant A's full-width dense tables + slide-over inspector drawer as the core shell,\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[?5W\u001b[J  \u001b[1mborrowing Variant B's collapsible Storage Location filter tree for the Catalog view and Variant C's interactive \u001b[m\r\n  \u001b[1mper-designator \u001b[94;22m[R1]\u001b[39;1m \u001b[94;22m[R2]\u001b[39;1m chips + side-by-side Bench Log for the Active Bench view).\u001b[m Full-width tables give maximum\r\n  breathing room for parametric columns, verbatim specs, and inline HTMX steppers, while sliding open the right-hand\r\n  inspector/catalog drawer on demand gives you Variant C's side-by-side kitting power without permanently cramping\r\n  the table columns. Does that combination match what you want?\r\n  ──────\r\n  \u001b[1m### Modern Web Guidance\u001b[m\r\n\n  • \u001b[94mresponsive-table\u001b[m: Wrapped data tables in focusable \u001b[94mrole=\"region\"\u001b[m containers with \u001b[94mcontainer-type: inline-size\u001b[m,\r\n  sticky column (\u001b[94mthead\u001b[m) and row (\u001b[94mtbody th\u001b[m) headers, and a \u001b[94m@container ("]
[0.000, "o", "width < 600px)\u001b[m stacked card transformation\r\n  using CSS custom properties for cell labels (\"Use \u001b[94m@container\u001b[m queries instead of \u001b[94m@media\u001b[m queries.\" / \u001b[94m\"/* MANDATORY:\u001b[m\r\n  \u001b[94mHide column header from layout and screen readers. */\"\u001b[m).\r\n  • \u001b[94mdialog\u001b[m: Used a native \u001b[94m<dialog closedby=\"any\">\u001b[m element with \u001b[94mshowModal()\u001b[m, scroll-containment rules on \u001b[94mdialog:modal\u001b[m\r\n  and \u001b[94mdialog::backdrop\u001b[m, a \u001b[94mclose\u001b[m listener that resets \u001b[94mdialog.returnValue = ''\u001b[m, and a pointer-bounds fallback when\r\n  \u001b[94mclosedBy\u001b[m is unsupported (\u001b[94m\"/* MANDATORY (both rules): without them, scrolling over the backdrop or inside the dialog\u001b[m\r\n  \u001b[94mscrolls the page behind it */\"\u001b[m / \u001b[94m\"DO read dialog.returnValue in a close listener to learn which button was used,\u001b[m\r\n  \u001b[94mthen reset it with dialog.returnValue = ''.\"\u001b[m).\r\n  • \u001b[94mdark-mode\u001b[m: Declared \u001b[94m<meta name=\"color-scheme\" content=\"light dark\">\u001b[m and \u001b[94m:root { color-scheme: light dark; }\u001b[m,\r\n  pairing \u001b[9"]
[0.000, "o", "4mlight-dark()\u001b[m color tokens with a \u001b[94m@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark)\u001b[m fallback so native scrollbars, form\r\n  controls, and surfaces adapt without flashes (\u001b[94m\"/* MANDATORY: Apply color-scheme to :root or html for viewport-wide\u001b[m\r\n  \u001b[94mtheming */\"\u001b[m / \u001b[94m\"/* MANDATORY: Fallback for browsers without light-dark support */\"\u001b[m).\r\n  • \u001b[94mbrand-consistent-forms\u001b[m: Applied high-contrast light/dark \u001b[94maccent-color\u001b[m tokens to native form controls and\r\n  progressive-enhancement fallback styles guarded by \u001b[94m@supports not (accent-color: var(--brand-color))\u001b[m (\u001b[94m\"You MUST use\u001b[m\r\n  \u001b[94mthe @supports not rule to apply custom fallback styles only when accent-color is not supported.\"\u001b[m).\r\n\n\u001b[90m────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[34;1m> please open the prototype in a browser\u001b[m\r\n⣾  \u001b[90mWorking...\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[90m──────────"]
