[0.083, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\u001b[?25l\u001b[0 q\u001b[29Aand \u001b[94mdialog::backdrop\u001b[m, a \u001b[94mclose\u001b[m listener that resets \u001b[94mdialog.returnValue = ''\u001b[m, and a pointer-bounds fallback when\u001b[K\r\n  \u001b[94mclosedBy\u001b[m is unsupported (\u001b[94m\"/* MANDATORY (both rules): without them, scrolling over the backdrop or inside the dialog\u001b[m\r\n  \u001b[94mscrolls the page behind it */\"\u001b[m / \u001b[94m\"DO read dialog.returnValue in a close listener to learn which button was used,\u001b[m\r\n  \u001b[94mthen reset it with dialog.returnValue = ''.\"\u001b[m).\r\n  • \u001b[94mdark-mode\u001b[m: Declared \u001b[94m<meta name=\"color-scheme\" content=\"light dark\">\u001b[m and \u001b[94m:root { color-scheme: light dark; }\u001b[m,\r\n  pairing \u001b[94mlight-dark()\u001b[m color tokens with a \u001b[94m@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark)\u001b[m fallback so native scrollbars, form\r\n  controls, and surfaces adapt without flashes (\u001b[94m\"/* MANDATORY: Apply color-scheme to :root or html for viewport-wide\u001b[m\r\n  \u001b[94mtheming */\"\u001b[m / \u001b[94m\"/* MANDATORY: Fallback for browsers without light-dark support */\"\u001b[m).\u001b[K\r\n  • \u001b[94mbrand-consistent-form"]
[0.000, "o", "s\u001b[m: Applied high-contrast light/dark \u001b[94maccent-color\u001b[m tokens to native form controls and\r\n  progressive-enhancement fallback styles guarded by \u001b[94m@supports not (accent-color: var(--brand-color))\u001b[m (\u001b[94m\"You MUST use\u001b[m\r\n  \u001b[94mthe @supports not rule to apply custom fallback styles only when accent-color is not supported.\"\u001b[m).\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[90m────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[34;1m> please open the prototype in a browser\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[33m●\u001b[m \u001b[33;1mRan\u001b[m \u001b[37m(open /Users/brett/Demos/audio-inventory-experiment/audio_inventory_skilled/.scratch/aud...)\u001b[m \u001b[37m(ctrl+o to expand)\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[33;1mCommand\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[90m───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────"]
[0.000, "o", "─────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[37;1mRequesting permission for:\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[37m   open\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[37m/Users/brett/Demos/audio-inventory-experiment/audio_inventory_skilled/.scratch/audio-inventory/prototype-ui.html\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[1mRun this command?\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[94m> 1. Yes, run command\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n  2. Yes, and always allow in this conversation for commands that start with 'open'\r\n  3. Yes, and always allow for commands that start with 'open' (Persist to settings.json)\r\n  4. No, cancel\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\n  \u001b[94;1m↑/↓\u001b[90;22m Navigate · \u001b[94;1mtab\u001b[90;22m Amend · \u001b[94;1mctrl+g\u001b[90;22m edit/expand command\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[?2026l"]
[2.224, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\u001b[0 q\r\u001b[30A  inspector/catalog drawer on demand gives you Variant C's side-by-side kitting power without permanently cramping\r\n  the table columns. Does that combination match what you want?\u001b[K\r\n  ──────\u001b[K\r\n  \u001b[1m### Modern Web Guidance\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\n  • \u001b[94mresponsive-table\u001b[m: Wrapped data tables in focusable \u001b[94mrole=\"region\"\u001b[m containers with \u001b[94mcontainer-type: inline-size\u001b[m,\u001b[K\r\n  sticky column (\u001b[94mthead\u001b[m) and row (\u001b[94mtbody th\u001b[m) headers, and a \u001b[94m@container (width < 600px)\u001b[m stacked card transformation\u001b[K\r\n  using CSS custom properties for cell labels (\"Use \u001b[94m@container\u001b[m queries instead of \u001b[94m@media\u001b[m queries.\" / \u001b[94m\"/* MANDATORY:\u001b[m\r\n  \u001b[94mHide column header from layout and screen readers. */\"\u001b[m).\u001b[K\r\n  • \u001b[94mdialog\u001b[m: Used a native \u001b[94m<dialog closedby=\"any\">\u001b[m element with \u001b[94mshowModal()\u001b[m, scroll-containment rules on \u001b[94mdialog:modal\u001b[m\r\n  and \u001b[94mdialog::backdrop\u001b[m, a \u001b[94mclose\u001b[m listener that resets \u001b[94mdialog.returnValue = ''\u001b[m, and "]
[0.000, "o", "a pointer-bounds fallback when\r\n  \u001b[94mclosedBy\u001b[m is unsupported (\u001b[94m\"/* MANDATORY (both rules): without them, scrolling over the backdrop or inside the dialog\u001b[m\r\n  \u001b[94mscrolls the page behind it */\"\u001b[m / \u001b[94m\"DO read dialog.returnValue in a close listener to learn which button was used,\u001b[m\r\n  \u001b[94mthen reset it with dialog.returnValue = ''.\"\u001b[m).\r\n  • \u001b[94mdark-mode\u001b[m: Declared \u001b[94m<meta name=\"color-scheme\" content=\"light dark\">\u001b[m and \u001b[94m:root { color-scheme: light dark; }\u001b[m,\r\n  pairing \u001b[94mlight-dark()\u001b[m color tokens with a \u001b[94m@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark)\u001b[m fallback so native scrollbars, form\u001b[K\r\n  controls, and surfaces adapt without flashes (\u001b[94m\"/* MANDATORY: Apply color-scheme to :root or html for viewport-wide\u001b[m\r\n  \u001b[94mtheming */\"\u001b[m / \u001b[94m\"/* MANDATORY: Fallback for browsers without light-dark support */\"\u001b[m).\r\n  • \u001b[94mbrand-consistent-forms\u001b[m: Applied high-contrast light/dark \u001b[94maccent-color\u001b[m tokens to native form controls and\u001b[K\r\n  progressive-enhancement fallba"]
[0.000, "o", "ck styles guarded by \u001b[94m@supports not (accent-color: var(--brand-color))\u001b[m (\u001b[94m\"You MUST use\u001b[m\r\n  \u001b[94mthe @supports not rule to apply custom fallback styles only when accent-color is not supported.\"\u001b[m).\r\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[90m────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[34;1m> please open the prototype in a browser\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[33m●\u001b[m \u001b[33;1mRunning\u001b[m \u001b[37m(open /Users/brett/Demos/audio-inventory-experiment/audio_inventory_skilled/.scratch...)\u001b[m \u001b[37m(ctrl+o to expand)\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n⣯  \u001b[90mRunn\u001b[94ming c\u001b[90mommand...\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[90m└ Tip: In /diff, press c to add inline comments and send them as feedback.\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[90m───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────"]
