[0.017, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\u001b[29AYou can switch between \u001b[1mVariant A\u001b[m, \u001b[1mVariant B\u001b[m, and \u001b[1mVariant C\u001b[m using the floating pill bar at the bottom of the screen\r\n  (or the \u001b[94m←\u001b[m and \u001b[94m→\u001b[m arrow keys), and click through the \u001b[1mCatalog\u001b[m, \u001b[1mKit Build BOM\u001b[m, and \u001b[1mBench Checklist\u001b[m views.\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\n  Once you've had a chance to click around:\r\n\u001b[K\u001b[?7l\n\u001b[K  ❓ \u001b[1mQ1\u001b[m — \u001b[1mOverall Workbench Layout & Navigation Structure\u001b[m: Does the recommended hybrid (\u001b[1mVariant A's\u001b[m full-width dense\u001b[?7h\u001b[117G\u001b[?7l\r\n\u001b[K  tables + slide-over inspector drawer as the core layout, combined with \u001b[1mVariant B's\u001b[m collapsible \u001b[1mStorage Location\u001b[?7h\u001b[114G\u001b[m\r\n  tree filter in the Catalog view and \u001b[1mVariant C's\u001b[m interactive per-designator \u001b[94m[R1]\u001b[m \u001b[94m[R2]\u001b[m chips + side-by-side \u001b[1mBench Log\u001b[m\r\n  in the Bench view) feel right, or do you prefer one of the other layouts?\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[90m─────────────────────────────────────────"]
[0.000, "o", "───────────────────\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[34;1m> A\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[37m▸ Thought for 13s\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[K\u001b[?7l\n\u001b[K  ❓ \u001b[1mQ2\u001b[m — \u001b[1mParametric Search Feedback & Multi-Lot Stock Adjustment in the Catalog Table\u001b[m: In Variant A's \u001b[1mComponent\u001b[?7h\u001b[113G\u001b[?7l\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[K  \u001b[1mCatalog\u001b[m view, how should live HTMX filtering and inline \u001b[1mStock Lot\u001b[m steppers behave?\u001b[?7h\u001b[85G\r\n\u001b[K\n  1. \u001b[1mDebounced HTMX Search (\u001b[94;22mdelay:150ms\u001b[39;1m) + Live Parsed Spec Badge + Single-Lot Inline Stepper / Multi-Lot Inspector\u001b[m\r\n  \u001b[1mDrawer\u001b[m:\u001b[K\r\n      • Typing in the search bar (\u001b[94mhx-get=\"/catalog\" hx-trigger=\"input changed delay:150ms\" hx-push-url=\"true\"\u001b[m)\r\n\u001b[6Cupdates the table and displays the live \u001b[94mspec_parser\u001b[39;1m interpretation badge\u001b[m (e.g., \u001b[94mValue: 4.7kΩ (4700 Ω) ·\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[6C\u001b[94mTolerance: 1%\u001b[m) so you can immediately see how shorthand like \u001b[94m4k7\u001b[m or \u001b[94m0.047uF\u001b[m was normalized, alongside dynamic\r\n\u001b[6Ccategory-specific attribute filters when a category is selected.\u001b[K"]
