[0.000, "o", "inline \u001b[94m− / qty / +\u001b[m stepper directly in the table cell (\u001b[94mhx-post\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[6Cswapping just that \u001b[94m<tr>\u001b[m), while rows with \u001b[1mmultiple Stock Lots\u001b[m render a \u001b[94m\"2 Stock Lots (57) ▸\"\u001b[m button that\r\n\u001b[6Ctargets the right-hand Inspector Drawer for per-location \u001b[94m− / +\u001b[m adjustments and 1-click \u001b[1mMerge Lots\u001b[m.\u001b[K\r\n  2. \u001b[1mInline Steppers for Every Lot Inside the Table Cell\u001b[m: Stack a separate \u001b[94m− / qty / +\u001b[m stepper for every \u001b[1mStorage\u001b[m\r\n  \u001b[1mLocation\u001b[m directly inside the table row even when a component has 3+ lots.\u001b[K\r\n  3. \u001b[1mDrawer-Only Adjustments\u001b[m: Never put \u001b[94m− / +\u001b[m steppers in the table row; require clicking into the right-hand\r\n  Inspector Drawer for all quantity changes.\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\u001b[?7l\n\u001b[K  ➡️ \u001b[1mRecommendation: Option 1 (Debounced HTMX search with live \u001b[94;22mspec_parser\u001b[39;1m token feedback, inline \u001b[94;22m− / +\u001b[39;1m stepper for\u001b[?7h\u001b[116G\u001b[?7l\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[K  \u001b[1msingle-lot components, and right-hand Inspector Drawer for multi-lot components and "]
