[0.017, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\r\u001b[29A\u001b[K\n\u001b[37m▸ Thought for 21s, 485 tokens\u001b[?7l\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[K\u001b[?7h\u001b[1G\u001b[?7l\n\u001b[K  ❓ \u001b[1mQ3\u001b[m — \u001b[1mKit Build BOM Allocation & Active Bench Checklist Interactions\u001b[m: For Variant A's \u001b[1mKit Build BOM\u001b[m and \u001b[1mActive\u001b[?7h\u001b[115G\u001b[m\r\n  \u001b[1mBench\u001b[m tabs, how should row transitions, batch kitting, and soldering progress work?\r\n\u001b[K\n  1. \u001b[1mRow-Level HTMX Transitions + Out-of-Band Readiness Summary + Per-Designator Bench Chips\u001b[m:\u001b[K\n\u001b[87D• \u001b[1mKit Build BOM Tab\u001b[m: Each \u001b[1mBOM Line\u001b[m \u001b[94m<tr>\u001b[m has inline 1-click \u001b[1mFulfillment Status\u001b[m pills (\u001b[94mUnallocated\u001b[m, \u001b[94mReserved\u001b[m,\r\n\u001b[6C\u001b[94mPicked\u001b[m, \u001b[94mInstalled\u001b[m) that swap the row via \u001b[94mhx-patch\u001b[m and update the build's readiness counter via \u001b[94mhx-swap-\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[6C\u001b[94moob=\"true\"\u001b[m, paired with top-level \u001b[1mBatch Kitting Actions\u001b[m (\u001b[94m\"Reserve All Available\"\u001b[m and \u001b[94m\"Pick All Reserved to\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[6C\u001b[94mProject Box\"\u001b[m). Clicking a row loads the right-hand \u001b[1mInspector Drawer\u001b[m for \u001b[94msource_lot_id\u001b[m selection, candida"]
[0.000, "o", "te\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[7Catching for \u001b[94mUnlinked\u001b[m lines, \u001b[1m1-Click Split BOM Line\u001b[m, and \u001b[1mSubstitute Catalog Component\u001b[m (via the native \u001b[94m<dialog>\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[6Cmodal).\u001b[K\n\u001b[7D• \u001b[1mActive Bench Checklist Tab\u001b[m: Groups \u001b[1mBOM Lines\u001b[m by assembly profile height (\u001b[94mStage 1: Low-Profile Resistors &\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[6C\u001b[94mDiodes\u001b[m, \u001b[94mStage 2: IC Sockets & Film Capacitors\u001b[m, \u001b[94mStage 3: Tall Caps, Pots & Off-Board Hardware\u001b[m), with \u001b[1mtappable\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[6C\u001b[1mper-designator chips\u001b[m (\u001b[94m[○ R1]\u001b[m, \u001b[94m[✓ R2]\u001b[m) that auto-transition the \u001b[1mBOM Line\u001b[m to \u001b[94mInstalled\u001b[m once every designator on\r\n\u001b[6Cthe row is checked (plus a 1-click \u001b[94m\"Mark All Installed\"\u001b[m button), alongside the pinned right-hand \u001b[1mBench Log &\u001b[m\r\n      \u001b[1mAttachments\u001b[m panel.\u001b[K\r\n  2. \u001b[1mRow-Only Checkboxes on the Bench (No Individual Designator Chips)\u001b[m: Only track whole-line \u001b[94mInstalled\u001b[m status on the\r\n  bench without individual \u001b[94m[R1]\u001b[m, \u001b[94m[R2]\u001b[m placement chips.\u001b[K\r\n  3. \u001b[1mCombined Single Tab for Kitti"]
[0.000, "o", "ng & Soldering\u001b[m: Merge the BOM Allocation table and the Active Bench Checklist into\r\n  a single table rather than separate \u001b[94mBOM & Allocation\u001b[m and \u001b[94mActive Bench Checklist\u001b[m tabs.\u001b[?7l\r\n\u001b[K\u001b[?7h\u001b[1G\u001b[?7l\n\u001b[K  ➡️ \u001b[1mRecommendation: Option 1 (Separate \u001b[94;22mBOM & Allocation\u001b[39;1m and \u001b[94;22mActive Bench Checklist\u001b[39;1m tabs, with inline HTMX status\u001b[?7h\u001b[114G\u001b[m\r\n  \u001b[1mpills + batch kitting actions + Inspector Drawer on the BOM tab, and stage-grouped rows with tappable per-\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n  \u001b[1mdesignator \u001b[94;22m[R1]\u001b[39;1m \u001b[94;22m[R2]\u001b[39;1m chips + pinned Bench Log on the Bench tab).\u001b[m Checking off individual reference designators (\u001b[94mR1\u001b[m,\r\n  \u001b[94mR2\u001b[m, \u001b[94mR5\u001b[m) prevents losing your place when soldering multi-quantity lines on a dense PCB. Does Option 1 lock this in?\r\n\u001b[K\n\n\n\n\u001b[90m? for shortcuts\u001b[m\u001b[2A\u001b[13D\u001b[?2026l"]
