[0.000, "o", "ore\u001b[m\n\u001b[44D\u001b[1K • \u001b[1mBlocked by\u001b[m: #5 (Active Bench Checklist, Build Attachments & Bench Log Entries)\n\u001b[81D\u001b[1K • \u001b[1mWhat it delivers\u001b[m: 1-click \u001b[1mDownload Backup (\u001b[94;22m.zip\u001b[39;1m)\u001b[m (\u001b[94mGET /settings/backup.zip\u001b[m) streaming a consistent snapshot\r\n\u001b[5C\u001b[1K of \u001b[94minventory.db\u001b[m and \u001b[94mattachments/\u001b[m, paired with an in-app and CLI restore workflow that unpacks a backup archive\r\n\u001b[5C\u001b[1K and verifies byte-for-byte preservation of database state and attachment files.\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\n  ──────\r\n  How does this breakdown look to you — specifically, does the granularity and dependency structure feel right, or\r\n  should any tickets be merged or split before I publish them?\u001b[K\r\n\n\u001b[90m────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[34;1m> go ahead\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[31m●\u001b[m \u001b[33;1mExplored\u001b[m 3 files \u001b[37m(prototype-ui.html, SKILL.md, SKILL.md)\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n\u001b["]
