[0.001, "o", "** ready-for-agent\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[37m  \u001b[90m 8 \u001b[39;48;2;14;52;15m \u001b[32m+  \u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[37m  \u001b[90m 9 \u001b[39;48;2;14;52;15m \u001b[32m+  \u001b[39m- [ ] A builder can open a native \u001b[38;2;151;198;123m`<dialog closedby=\"any\">`\u001b[39m substitution modal from any **BOM Line** (or the\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[4C\u001b[37m\u001b[1K \u001b[48;2;14;52;15m \u001b[32m   \u001b[39mInspector Drawer) to link any catalog **Component** and record an optional \u001b[38;2;151;198;123m`substitution_note`\u001b[39m without\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[4C\u001b[37m\u001b[1K \u001b[48;2;14;52;15m \u001b[32m   \u001b[39moverwriting \u001b[38;2;151;198;123m`raw_spec_text`\u001b[39m, rendering both the original schematic specification (e.g., \u001b[38;2;151;198;123m`J201`\u001b[39m) and the\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[4C\u001b[37m\u001b[1K \u001b[48;2;14;52;15m \u001b[32m   \u001b[39msubstituted part + note (e.g., \u001b[38;2;151;198;123m`2N5457 — pinout rotated`\u001b[39m) side by side in the **BOM** table.\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[37m  \u001b[90m10 \u001b[39;48;2;14;52;15m \u001b[32m+  \u001b[39m- [ ] A builder can partially allocate a **BOM Line** (\u001b[38;2;151;198;123m`0 < quantity_allocated < quantity_required`\u001b[39m) when\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[4C\u001b[37m\u001b[1K \u001b[48"]
