[0.101, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\r\u001b[29A\u001b[K\n\u001b[32m●\u001b[m \u001b[33;1mScheduled\u001b[m 1 timer \u001b[37m(10s: Check if Spec review subagent has completed.)\u001b[m \u001b[37m(ctrl+o to expand)\u001b[m\r\n\n  Waiting for the Spec axis review subagent to complete.\u001b[K\r\n\n\u001b[32m●\u001b[m \u001b[33;1mMessaged\u001b[m 1 subagent \u001b[37m(ctrl+o to expand)\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n\n  \u001b[94mCode Review - Spec Axis\u001b[m is still running (\u001b[94mview_file\u001b[m). Let's end our turn and wait for its notification.\r\n\n  Both \u001b[1mStandards\u001b[m and \u001b[1mSpec\u001b[m review subagents have completed their analyses!\u001b[K\r\n  Let's review the findings across both axes and follow Step 7 of \u001b[94m/implement-spec\u001b[m:\r\n  \"7. Once all tickets are complete, call the Skill tool with \u001b[94mcode-review\u001b[m on the integration branch. Fix all issues\r\n  raised by the code review in a single fresh \u001b[1mimplementer subagent\u001b[m.\"\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\n  Let's create a fresh git worktree (\u001b[94mticket-review-fixes\u001b[m) based on \u001b[94mfeat/audio-inventory\u001b[m (\u001b[94mb92ba8a\u001b[m), launch a fresh\r\n  implementer subagent to fix every single issue raised by both the \u001b[1mStandards\u001b[m "]
[0.000, "o", "and \u001b[1mSpec\u001b[m reviews, and then merge it\r\n  back into \u001b[94mfeat/audio-inventory\u001b[m!\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[32m●\u001b[m \u001b[33;1mRan\u001b[m \u001b[37m(git worktree add -b ticket-review-fixes /tmp/audio-inventory-wt/ticket-review-fixes fea...)\u001b[m \u001b[37m(ctrl+o to expand)\u001b[m\r\n\n  Let's launch a single fresh \u001b[1mimplementer subagent\u001b[m in \u001b[94m/tmp/audio-inventory-wt/ticket-review-fixes\u001b[m to fix all issues\u001b[K\r\n  raised by the \u001b[1mStandards\u001b[m and \u001b[1mSpec\u001b[m code reviews!\r\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[32m●\u001b[m \u001b[33;1mSpawned\u001b[m 1 subagent \u001b[37m(ctrl+o to expand)\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n⡿  \u001b[94mDeleg\u001b[90mating...\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[90m└ Tip: Use /fork to branch the conversation from an earlier point.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[90m────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[94m>\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n\n  \u001b"]
